WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.290
Okay, welcome to Nagarjuna course three.

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:09.290
We are going through
five years of Nagarjuna.

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:14.440
I always wanted to
translate his greatest book,

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:15.870
which is called "Wisdom",

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:16.737
or "Prajna".

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:21.120
So, I just decided that

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.250
during the Lam Rim times,

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:26.370
maybe I would give you guys some dessert.

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:29.520
And you know what happens
if you get too much dessert,

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:30.423
you get crazy.

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:34.993
So, we'd been filming
Nagarjuna number three.

00:00:34.993 --> 00:00:37.543
It's going to take five
years to finish Nagarjuna.

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:40.260
And we're on the third year now.

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:42.520
And it's going well.

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:45.720
We are working on Choney
Lama's commentary.

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:47.330
Two good things happened yesterday.

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:49.580
You guys are going to
ask me what they were?

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:50.450
- [Students] What are they?

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:55.450
- Number one, we found the scan

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:57.340
of Choney Lama's commentary

00:00:57.340 --> 00:00:59.510
that got lost 20 years ago

00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:02.230
that came from his own monastery,

00:01:02.230 --> 00:01:03.920
from Choney Monastery.

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:06.930
And so now I can actually check things.

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:09.240
And it was the only copy in the world.

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:11.053
And we can talk about that someday.

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:13.293
And secondly,

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:15.033
are you ready?

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:18.540
Peach Tree Cafe got all its permits

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:19.851
from the county

00:01:19.851 --> 00:01:22.851
[audience applause]

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:28.610
after one and a half years of fighting.

00:01:28.610 --> 00:01:30.000
I almost had a heart attack.

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:34.650
I don't know why they did
it, but God bless them.

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:36.930
So, I'm feeling good today.

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:39.560
I thought that since a
lot of you guys listening,

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:41.840
first of all, I'd like to thank you

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:44.220
for being the ACI volunteer team

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:46.190
and working all over the world

00:01:46.190 --> 00:01:48.480
and making things happen for ACI.

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:50.080
I'm really, really grateful.

00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:53.570
Say again?

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:55.970
Oh, we got Medicine Buddha volunteers too.

00:01:55.970 --> 00:01:59.090
So, I was thinking what's a tasty dish

00:01:59.090 --> 00:02:02.350
to serve up from Peach Tree Cafe

00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:04.340
for ACI volunteers

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:07.670
and Medicine Buddha volunteers together.

00:02:07.670 --> 00:02:10.773
What's something delicious
that I can give you?

00:02:10.773 --> 00:02:14.160
Because that's what a
cafe owner has to do.

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:18.020
So, I thought a lot of
you are in the Gold Clubs.

00:02:18.020 --> 00:02:21.450
A lot of you are helping
to support the project

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:23.310
to save the ancient books.

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:28.217
It will take about 700
years to save all the books

00:02:28.217 --> 00:02:30.270
and it will take about, I don't know...

00:02:30.270 --> 00:02:33.010
Just one book that we started this year,

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:34.870
is going to take 51 years to finish.

00:02:34.870 --> 00:02:36.543
I don't know what's going to happen.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:40.330
So, we've been working like that.

00:02:40.330 --> 00:02:43.040
And I thought that since
a lot of you are involved

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:45.017
with ACIP...oh, ALL,

00:02:46.110 --> 00:02:48.000
and how to save the books,

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:48.970
I thought today,

00:02:48.970 --> 00:02:51.190
maybe it would be fun to start out

00:02:52.470 --> 00:02:56.730
with describing to you how I use it.

00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:58.490
So, I use this database

00:02:59.390 --> 00:03:02.280
about 200-300 times every day

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:04.810
for the last 35 years.

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:07.310
And without it,

00:03:07.310 --> 00:03:09.740
it'd be very difficult for me to teach.

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:11.310
What I'd like to do...

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:13.435
And we're sorry, our tech
is not too high today.

00:03:13.435 --> 00:03:15.622
I'm holding one computer on my lap,

00:03:15.622 --> 00:03:19.290
and I'm facing it to this other computer.

00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:21.490
But I thought you'd like to see

00:03:21.490 --> 00:03:23.040
what the database looks like,

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:27.410
because a lot of you
guys are raising money

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:29.470
for producing this database

00:03:29.470 --> 00:03:33.060
and maybe you've never seen it in use.

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:35.860
And I sort of want to tie
it in to Nagarjuna today.

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:38.920
So, this is a special Nagarjuna class.

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:41.630
And during this version of Nagarjuna,

00:03:41.630 --> 00:03:43.893
which is very, very difficult,

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:49.990
we are tying it into why
does Medicine Buddha work.

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:53.273
Why did the mantras work?

00:03:53.273 --> 00:03:56.167
How does that tantra work?

00:03:56.167 --> 00:03:59.750
And if you understand
how the mantras work,

00:04:00.797 --> 00:04:02.820
how the practice works,

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:05.170
then it's going to work a lot better.

00:04:05.170 --> 00:04:07.460
It's like a computer system.

00:04:07.460 --> 00:04:09.810
If you understand how it works,

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:11.010
it can work better.

00:04:11.010 --> 00:04:13.200
And if you don't understand how it works,

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:15.560
you could end up holding
a computer on your lap

00:04:15.560 --> 00:04:18.773
to try to get the other screen to show.

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:24.160
So obviously, it's really useful

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:25.800
to know how something works.

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:28.790
So, if you understand

00:04:28.790 --> 00:04:31.203
how the Medicine Buddha practice works,

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:34.270
then you can do it a lot better

00:04:34.270 --> 00:04:37.140
and you can get better results from it.

00:04:37.140 --> 00:04:39.510
We had a big discussion about it.

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:40.343
Some people were saying,

00:04:40.343 --> 00:04:42.180
"Oh, it doesn't matter how it works.

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:43.767
Just teach them how to do it."

00:04:43.767 --> 00:04:47.480
But I do believe that if
you know how it works,

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:49.140
it's more powerful.

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:51.900
If you're like an old grandma somewhere

00:04:51.900 --> 00:04:54.210
and you just want to do mantras

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:56.200
and you don't want to know how they work,

00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:57.163
that's okay.

00:04:58.140 --> 00:05:00.453
I'm thinking about my mom, she's 95.

00:05:03.230 --> 00:05:04.950
Maybe I can't explain to her

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:05.840
how the mantra works.

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:08.520
I can just tell her,
"Just do the mantras."

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:10.130
But if you understand how things work,

00:05:10.130 --> 00:05:11.740
they work better.

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:12.810
So, here's the database.

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:14.090
Here's what it looks like.

00:05:14.090 --> 00:05:19.090
Let's say I wanted to show
you something about Nagarjuna.

00:05:19.420 --> 00:05:23.760
Of course, Nagarjuna's thing
is to explain emptiness.

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:27.340
Nagarjuna's most popular thing of all time

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:29.720
is to explain emptiness, of course.

00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:33.280
And here's what the database looks like

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:35.400
on my computer.

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:39.230
Here's the different parts of the database

00:05:39.230 --> 00:05:41.150
that I use everyday.

00:05:41.150 --> 00:05:43.630
And I wanted to take you, I don't know,

00:05:43.630 --> 00:05:44.933
let's go to the Tengyur.

00:05:45.880 --> 00:05:49.880
This is 5,000 books that were

00:05:51.690 --> 00:05:53.520
translated into Tibetan

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:56.780
and the translation took 700 years.

00:05:56.780 --> 00:05:58.750
They finished it around the time

00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:00.480
of Je Tsongkapa.

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:05.480
And it was 4,600 or 4,700 books.

00:06:06.750 --> 00:06:10.010
And the first goal of ACIP...ALL

00:06:10.010 --> 00:06:11.570
35 years ago,

00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:15.450
was to input all their
ancient books from India,

00:06:15.450 --> 00:06:17.150
which is all the sutras,

00:06:17.150 --> 00:06:20.060
and all the commentaries,
and all the tantras.

00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:22.220
The only problem was,

00:06:22.220 --> 00:06:25.580
there was no copy in India of them.

00:06:25.580 --> 00:06:28.380
They all got burned or destroyed.

00:06:28.380 --> 00:06:31.080
So, the first job we had was to...

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:35.540
We actually contacted this
ancient, ancient monastery

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:37.810
that still had some blocks.

00:06:37.810 --> 00:06:40.740
And we actually got into the library

00:06:40.740 --> 00:06:43.040
and we had the blocks.

00:06:43.040 --> 00:06:45.970
We had new pages printed from the blocks.

00:06:45.970 --> 00:06:49.143
You're talking about 310,000 blocks.

00:06:54.827 --> 00:06:57.690
310,000 blocks

00:06:57.690 --> 00:07:00.470
to print all the things
from the Kangyur and Tengyur

00:07:00.470 --> 00:07:02.160
from ancient India.

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:03.860
And we did it.

00:07:03.860 --> 00:07:07.700
We finished. It took us about 10-12 years.

00:07:07.700 --> 00:07:08.953
And we typed,

00:07:11.601 --> 00:07:14.460
it's about 310,000 pages,

00:07:14.460 --> 00:07:15.323
and we did it.

00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:18.810
So, we have that what we can use.

00:07:18.810 --> 00:07:20.620
Here's Tengyur.

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:23.400
These are all the commentaries
from ancient India.

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:24.370
And I wanted to...

00:07:24.370 --> 00:07:28.033
Here's all the categories
of the Tengyur here.

00:07:28.900 --> 00:07:33.617
For example, there's Perfection
of Wisdom, Middle Way,

00:07:34.470 --> 00:07:37.007
there's Mind-Only, there's Abhidharma,

00:07:37.900 --> 00:07:39.530
there's Vinaya,

00:07:39.530 --> 00:07:40.873
there's Logic,

00:07:41.710 --> 00:07:43.390
there's medicine,

00:07:43.390 --> 00:07:44.960
there's architecture,

00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:46.333
there's grammar.

00:07:49.688 --> 00:07:51.850
There's books about how
to do practical things

00:07:51.850 --> 00:07:53.900
like run a government.

00:07:53.900 --> 00:07:55.300
There's even a book in here about

00:07:55.300 --> 00:07:57.103
how to grade gemstones,

00:07:58.110 --> 00:07:59.880
which was the most fun for me.

00:07:59.880 --> 00:08:02.220
I wanted to show you these category,

00:08:02.220 --> 00:08:03.053
the second one here,

00:08:03.053 --> 00:08:05.460
which is called Vajrayana,

00:08:05.460 --> 00:08:07.000
the Diamond Way.

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:10.030
And as you can see, it's almost...

00:08:10.030 --> 00:08:12.160
Well, it's 78 different volumes,

00:08:12.160 --> 00:08:14.440
which means 78,000 pages

00:08:14.440 --> 00:08:17.380
of ancient commentaries

00:08:17.380 --> 00:08:18.213
to the tantras.

00:08:18.213 --> 00:08:23.190
The tantras are about 500,000 pages,

00:08:23.190 --> 00:08:27.410
but here you've got about 78,000 pages

00:08:27.410 --> 00:08:29.300
of commentary to them.

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:33.330
And these are divided.

00:08:33.330 --> 00:08:34.480
By the way,

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:37.720
the arrangement of the
Vajrayana was secret,

00:08:37.720 --> 00:08:41.010
and me and Venerable Jigme figured it out

00:08:41.010 --> 00:08:43.860
using an ancient commentary that we found.

00:08:43.860 --> 00:08:46.960
It was really a big, big deal

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:49.090
that after, I don't know,

00:08:49.090 --> 00:08:52.590
this was carved 300-400 years ago,

00:08:52.590 --> 00:08:56.660
somebody figured out
how they put the tantras

00:08:56.660 --> 00:08:58.170
in the order that they are,

00:08:58.170 --> 00:08:59.850
which is really awesome.

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:01.680
I don't know if you can see,

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:05.600
but here are the four classes of tantra.

00:09:05.600 --> 00:09:07.763
There are four different levels of tantra.

00:09:08.660 --> 00:09:11.830
For example, Medicine
Buddha is the fourth level

00:09:11.830 --> 00:09:14.833
and highest level is called 'Anuttara'.

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:17.090
First level.

00:09:17.090 --> 00:09:19.380
And let's go to Anuttara.

00:09:19.380 --> 00:09:21.620
Here's, I don't know,

00:09:21.620 --> 00:09:25.600
17 different categories

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:27.330
of different Anuttara Tantras.

00:09:27.330 --> 00:09:30.810
For example, Chakrasamvara is here.

00:09:30.810 --> 00:09:32.893
Kalachakra is here.

00:09:33.820 --> 00:09:37.380
One part of Tara is here.

00:09:37.380 --> 00:09:40.080
Perhaps the highest tantra

00:09:40.080 --> 00:09:41.340
is called Guhyasamaja,

00:09:42.580 --> 00:09:45.380
and this was the favorite of Je Tsongkapa.

00:09:45.380 --> 00:09:47.540
And this is also the one that's used

00:09:47.540 --> 00:09:48.720
for the tantric college,

00:09:48.720 --> 00:09:53.720
where my teacher was the
assistant director in 1955.

00:09:55.830 --> 00:10:00.830
If you go inside of the
Guhyasamaja secret books,

00:10:01.840 --> 00:10:06.360
there's five huge categories
and hundreds of books.

00:10:06.360 --> 00:10:10.890
The first category is
called KLU SGRUB LUGS

00:10:10.890 --> 00:10:15.890
which means the system of Nagarjuna.

00:10:16.080 --> 00:10:17.377
So, people ask me,

00:10:17.377 --> 00:10:20.480
"Hey, did Nagarjuna know about tantra?"

00:10:20.480 --> 00:10:22.480
Hey, the highest part

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:26.510
of the highest tantras is Nagarjuna.

00:10:26.510 --> 00:10:28.010
And it's all dedicated to him.

00:10:28.010 --> 00:10:30.180
It's 50 volumes

00:10:31.040 --> 00:10:34.470
dedicated to Nagarjuna's interpretation

00:10:34.470 --> 00:10:36.974
of the Diamond Way.

00:10:36.974 --> 00:10:40.230
And he's the first person
mentioned in the Tengyur.

00:10:40.230 --> 00:10:42.410
So, he's the greatest expert,

00:10:42.410 --> 00:10:44.200
not only about emptiness,

00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:46.320
but he's the greatest expert,

00:10:46.320 --> 00:10:51.320
as you can see here, in
the secret teachings.

00:10:51.700 --> 00:10:52.767
He's number one.

00:10:53.630 --> 00:10:57.020
He was the highest teacher

00:10:57.020 --> 00:10:59.110
and his system was recorded

00:10:59.110 --> 00:11:01.430
and used in ancient India.

00:11:01.430 --> 00:11:05.000
And there still exist a
couple of thousand pages

00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:08.140
of explanation of his version

00:11:08.140 --> 00:11:09.440
of the Guhyasamaja,

00:11:09.440 --> 00:11:12.690
which is again Tsongkapa's favorite

00:11:14.210 --> 00:11:16.310
tantra that he used himself.

00:11:16.310 --> 00:11:18.800
So, there's the books from ancient India,

00:11:18.800 --> 00:11:22.030
and the first grade emphasis
of the secret teachings,

00:11:22.030 --> 00:11:25.310
of the highest class of
the secret teachings,

00:11:25.310 --> 00:11:27.130
is Nagarjuna's system,

00:11:27.130 --> 00:11:28.720
Nagarjuna's presentation,

00:11:28.720 --> 00:11:31.100
which is very, very beautiful.

00:11:31.100 --> 00:11:36.100
Now, suppose I'm working with the database

00:11:36.170 --> 00:11:38.060
and I want to see...

00:11:38.060 --> 00:11:40.890
Well, what did the Tibetans...

00:11:40.890 --> 00:11:44.330
The Tibetans made a thousand
years of commentaries,

00:11:44.330 --> 00:11:49.050
what did they say about
Nagarjuna's treatment

00:11:49.050 --> 00:11:50.810
of the secret way,

00:11:50.810 --> 00:11:51.643
the Diamond Way?

00:11:51.643 --> 00:11:52.610
So then, in the database,

00:11:52.610 --> 00:11:55.490
I would go to GSUNG 'BUM,

00:11:55.490 --> 00:11:59.040
which means here's all the Tibetan books.

00:11:59.040 --> 00:11:59.873
And I don't know,

00:11:59.873 --> 00:12:02.873
we have something like
50,000 books finished.

00:12:03.980 --> 00:12:05.990
And here you can say,

00:12:05.990 --> 00:12:07.113
I clicked on BLO SBYONG,

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:10.540
and on the right,

00:12:10.540 --> 00:12:12.120
you can see all the books.

00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:14.000
Actually, it's all the shelves

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:17.140
of our digital library
that have BLO SBYONGs.

00:12:17.140 --> 00:12:20.283
There's about 150 BLO SBYONGs there.

00:12:21.210 --> 00:12:25.890
And by the way, it took 35
years of really hard work.

00:12:25.890 --> 00:12:27.700
First of all, to find the books,

00:12:27.700 --> 00:12:30.280
then to input the books.

00:12:30.280 --> 00:12:34.780
And no one in history has cataloged them.

00:12:34.780 --> 00:12:35.990
Nobody.

00:12:35.990 --> 00:12:37.310
And we cataloged them.

00:12:37.310 --> 00:12:40.550
It took about 30 years of work.

00:12:40.550 --> 00:12:42.860
So, we don't talk about it much.

00:12:42.860 --> 00:12:44.270
You guys probably never heard about it.

00:12:44.270 --> 00:12:47.150
But it took thousands of hours of work

00:12:48.800 --> 00:12:50.640
to put the library into order,

00:12:50.640 --> 00:12:52.160
to put everything on shelves,

00:12:52.160 --> 00:12:54.850
to say, "Oh, tantra is over here.

00:12:54.850 --> 00:12:55.959
Middle Way is over here.

00:12:55.959 --> 00:12:57.360
Abhidharma is over there."

00:12:57.360 --> 00:12:58.960
And then to arrange all the shelves.

00:12:58.960 --> 00:13:02.090
It took many, many, thousands of hours.

00:13:02.090 --> 00:13:04.140
So, let's go to tantra.

00:13:04.140 --> 00:13:09.140
Let's just see how did the
Tibetans deal with tantra?

00:13:10.000 --> 00:13:12.210
So, it happens to be...

00:13:12.210 --> 00:13:13.043
And by the way,

00:13:13.043 --> 00:13:14.020
you can see all the categories here:

00:13:14.020 --> 00:13:17.490
Vinaya, there is lineage trees,

00:13:17.490 --> 00:13:19.410
there is history books,

00:13:19.410 --> 00:13:20.693
Middle Way,

00:13:22.700 --> 00:13:25.043
comparative philosophy, Abhidharma.

00:13:26.020 --> 00:13:27.330
So, let's go to the tantra,

00:13:27.330 --> 00:13:28.617
which is called RGYUD.

00:13:29.640 --> 00:13:30.930
And on the right,

00:13:30.930 --> 00:13:35.930
you can see all of the
different tantric systems.

00:13:36.280 --> 00:13:38.103
There's 130.

00:13:39.120 --> 00:13:40.500
Medicine Buddha is one.

00:13:41.868 --> 00:13:45.567
And there's 129 others
that we have preserved.

00:13:47.630 --> 00:13:51.420
So, you can see here,
for example, Manjushri,

00:13:51.420 --> 00:13:54.453
White Manjushri, Chakrasamvara, Amitabha.

00:13:55.970 --> 00:13:57.550
We have cataloged,

00:13:58.450 --> 00:14:03.450
and we have saved 130
different schools of tantra.

00:14:04.410 --> 00:14:07.575
So, Medicine Buddha is
just one school of tantra.

00:14:07.575 --> 00:14:09.080
Then there's 129 others

00:14:09.080 --> 00:14:11.000
that we have identified

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:12.233
and we have recovered.

00:14:13.690 --> 00:14:16.280
So, if you look here...

00:14:16.280 --> 00:14:17.353
Let's go to that

00:14:18.732 --> 00:14:21.300
Nagarjuna's presentation

00:14:21.300 --> 00:14:22.810
of the highest tantra

00:14:22.810 --> 00:14:24.360
which is called Guhyasamaja

00:14:25.990 --> 00:14:29.250
and it's right here.

00:14:29.250 --> 00:14:32.930
Then you can see on the right here

00:14:32.930 --> 00:14:35.120
are all the different categories

00:14:35.120 --> 00:14:39.217
of the Guhyasamaja and commentaries:

00:14:42.165 --> 00:14:46.643
how to move your mind on after you die,

00:14:47.610 --> 00:14:51.180
how to do the guru
yoga, how to do retreat,

00:14:51.180 --> 00:14:52.640
how to do the empowerment,

00:14:52.640 --> 00:14:53.840
how to draw the mandala,

00:14:55.010 --> 00:14:56.823
how to make the tormas,

00:14:59.440 --> 00:15:01.310
how to do the mantras,

00:15:01.310 --> 00:15:02.520
how to do the confession,

00:15:02.520 --> 00:15:05.770
how to do the four powers
according to Guhyasamaja,

00:15:05.770 --> 00:15:07.170
how to do the fire offering,

00:15:09.040 --> 00:15:11.670
and many, many categories like that.

00:15:11.670 --> 00:15:14.270
So, that's just Nagarjuna.

00:15:14.270 --> 00:15:17.490
That's just Nagarjuna's tantra.

00:15:17.490 --> 00:15:18.990
And let's check...

00:15:21.360 --> 00:15:25.183
Let's see how many pages are there.

00:15:28.430 --> 00:15:31.983
So, it's seven million bytes,

00:15:32.990 --> 00:15:35.460
Seven million bytes.

00:15:35.460 --> 00:15:38.620
Call it, I don't know...

00:15:38.620 --> 00:15:40.473
If you transfer it into pages,

00:15:41.870 --> 00:15:46.870
it's 7.5 megabytes just on Nagarjuna.

00:15:50.820 --> 00:15:52.673
It's about 5,000 pages.

00:15:52.673 --> 00:15:57.020
5,000 pages of Nagarjuna's explanation

00:15:57.020 --> 00:15:58.420
of the secret teachings.

00:15:58.420 --> 00:16:01.060
Why are we talking about all this?

00:16:01.060 --> 00:16:03.170
Well, as maybe you noticed,

00:16:04.274 --> 00:16:09.274
Nagarjuna made the ritual that we used

00:16:09.510 --> 00:16:11.730
to take our Bodhisattva vows.

00:16:11.730 --> 00:16:14.030
Without that ritual,

00:16:14.030 --> 00:16:15.670
without some ritual

00:16:15.670 --> 00:16:17.150
for the Bodhisattva vows,

00:16:17.150 --> 00:16:20.140
you're not allowed to
study Medicine Buddha.

00:16:20.140 --> 00:16:22.110
You have to take an empowerment

00:16:22.110 --> 00:16:23.870
and then you have to take the vows,

00:16:23.870 --> 00:16:26.433
at least a vow to try to be Bodhisattva.

00:16:28.200 --> 00:16:29.900
You have to go through that ceremony.

00:16:29.900 --> 00:16:33.190
And we used Nagarjuna's ceremony.

00:16:33.190 --> 00:16:37.830
Now today we're going to
jump into the swimming pool

00:16:37.830 --> 00:16:39.160
called Nagarjuna,

00:16:39.160 --> 00:16:41.773
and it's extremely hard.

00:16:42.950 --> 00:16:45.960
We're going to be jumping into

00:16:45.960 --> 00:16:49.226
his teachings on emptiness.

00:16:49.226 --> 00:16:51.640
- Geshe-la, what's it got
to do with Medicine Buddha?

00:16:51.640 --> 00:16:55.030
- Well, here's the search
program for the database.

00:16:55.030 --> 00:16:57.650
We invented this search program.

00:16:59.610 --> 00:17:01.860
I thought you'd like to see how it works.

00:17:01.860 --> 00:17:06.860
I'm going to search 5,000
books from ancient India.

00:17:07.050 --> 00:17:10.583
I'm going to look for any presentation of

00:17:10.583 --> 00:17:14.070
BYANG CHUB KYI SEMS, of Bodhichitta,

00:17:14.070 --> 00:17:18.300
and I just used a part of
the name because it's faster.

00:17:18.300 --> 00:17:22.030
And then I'm going to look
at it near his name, Naga.

00:17:22.030 --> 00:17:26.512
Did Nagarjuna write
anything about Bodhichitta?

00:17:26.512 --> 00:17:29.870
- Why, Geshe-la, why are
you off to Bodhichitta now?

00:17:29.870 --> 00:17:31.580
- Because I'm irritated.

00:17:31.580 --> 00:17:32.680
- Why are you irritated?

00:17:32.680 --> 00:17:34.040
- Because I'm aggravated.

00:17:34.040 --> 00:17:35.640
- Why you aggravated?

00:17:35.640 --> 00:17:36.930
- I talked to somebody yesterday.

00:17:36.930 --> 00:17:39.930
They said, "Oh, we went
on to Medicine Buddha,

00:17:39.930 --> 00:17:42.010
"we don't need Lam Rim anymore.

00:17:42.010 --> 00:17:43.550
"We're advanced now.

00:17:43.550 --> 00:17:45.370
We don't have to do Lam Rim."

00:17:45.370 --> 00:17:48.133
And I'm like, [growls] I got aggravated.

00:17:49.400 --> 00:17:53.140
So the person who wrote

00:17:54.863 --> 00:17:59.460
8,000 pages of commentary based on him

00:17:59.460 --> 00:18:00.640
and some by him

00:18:01.700 --> 00:18:04.063
on the highest teachings of tantra -

00:18:05.700 --> 00:18:08.360
did he study Lam Rim?

00:18:08.360 --> 00:18:11.330
Did he think Lam Rim was still important

00:18:11.330 --> 00:18:13.970
or did he just go on to Medicine Buddha?

00:18:13.970 --> 00:18:14.803
Well, here it is.

00:18:14.803 --> 00:18:16.340
You can ask the database.

00:18:16.340 --> 00:18:17.340
"Hey, database.

00:18:17.340 --> 00:18:18.173
Sorry.

00:18:19.040 --> 00:18:22.633
Did Nagarjuna think
Bodhichitta was important?"

00:18:23.860 --> 00:18:25.070
And then you can look.

00:18:25.070 --> 00:18:28.600
You going to search, I don't know,

00:18:28.600 --> 00:18:31.610
a million pages in one and a half seconds.

00:18:31.610 --> 00:18:32.600
Are you ready? Are you watching?

00:18:32.600 --> 00:18:33.433
Here we go.

00:18:33.433 --> 00:18:36.270
One, two, three, found!

00:18:36.270 --> 00:18:37.540
Found it.

00:18:37.540 --> 00:18:40.100
It took less than a second I guess.

00:18:40.100 --> 00:18:41.996
And there it is.

00:18:41.996 --> 00:18:44.510
KLU SGRUB means Nagarjuna.

00:18:44.510 --> 00:18:46.615
And here's the book called

00:18:46.615 --> 00:18:48.410
BYANG CHUB KYI SEMS BSKYED PA'I CHO GA

00:18:48.410 --> 00:18:49.440
Yes.

00:18:49.440 --> 00:18:51.490
He wrote a ritual

00:18:51.490 --> 00:18:53.640
for taking the bodhisattva vows

00:18:53.640 --> 00:18:55.750
and it's in the ancient books.

00:18:55.750 --> 00:18:58.190
Did he write anything else?

00:18:58.190 --> 00:18:59.190
Yeah.

00:18:59.190 --> 00:19:00.610
He wrote this:

00:19:00.610 --> 00:19:03.810
a commentary on how to get bodhichitta.

00:19:03.810 --> 00:19:08.662
He wrote a commentary on
how to get bodhichitta.

00:19:08.662 --> 00:19:11.098
Where is that commentary located?

00:19:11.098 --> 00:19:12.348
In the tantras.

00:19:15.572 --> 00:19:16.405
Okay?

00:19:16.405 --> 00:19:18.007
Nagarjuna's commentary

00:19:18.007 --> 00:19:20.230
on how to get bodhichitta

00:19:20.230 --> 00:19:21.093
is tantric.

00:19:22.010 --> 00:19:23.590
It's in the tantra.

00:19:23.590 --> 00:19:24.600
I didn't say so.

00:19:24.600 --> 00:19:25.433
They said so.

00:19:25.433 --> 00:19:30.180
So, now you've got 8,000
pages of tantric commentaries

00:19:31.300 --> 00:19:36.000
and root texts about
Nagarjuna's system on tantra.

00:19:36.000 --> 00:19:38.567
Maybe he understands Medicine Buddha.

00:19:40.380 --> 00:19:41.800
Maybe he thought it was important

00:19:41.800 --> 00:19:44.283
to take your bodhisattva
vows as part of tantra.

00:19:45.610 --> 00:19:46.913
He wrote the book!

00:19:47.880 --> 00:19:49.530
He wrote the book, okay?

00:19:49.530 --> 00:19:52.522
So I just wanted to impress on you guys,

00:19:52.522 --> 00:19:55.180
there's a huge connection.

00:19:55.180 --> 00:19:57.780
You've got to study Lam Rim

00:19:57.780 --> 00:20:00.220
if you want to study tantra,

00:20:00.220 --> 00:20:01.600
Medicine Buddha.

00:20:01.600 --> 00:20:04.710
And especially the part of the Lam Rim

00:20:04.710 --> 00:20:07.650
that deals with compassion and love,

00:20:07.650 --> 00:20:11.460
and especially the part about emptiness.

00:20:11.460 --> 00:20:13.440
You've got to understand emptiness,

00:20:14.640 --> 00:20:16.640
or the mantra doesn't work.

00:20:16.640 --> 00:20:18.130
You can sit and do mantras all day,

00:20:18.130 --> 00:20:21.763
but if you don't understand
how something works,

00:20:22.680 --> 00:20:24.240
it doesn't work.

00:20:24.240 --> 00:20:25.370
It's weird.

00:20:25.370 --> 00:20:27.080
You can say mantras, it's okay.

00:20:27.080 --> 00:20:28.430
You get a little good karma

00:20:29.810 --> 00:20:31.490
because of your motivation.

00:20:31.490 --> 00:20:36.490
But if you go and fight your way through

00:20:36.910 --> 00:20:39.280
Nagarjuna's presentation on emptiness,

00:20:39.280 --> 00:20:42.050
then you're really going to
understand Medicine Buddha.

00:20:42.050 --> 00:20:43.543
So we call this program

00:20:44.770 --> 00:20:46.800
'The Emptiness of Medicine Buddha',

00:20:46.800 --> 00:20:50.840
and let's jump into the
emptiness of Medicine Buddha.

00:20:50.840 --> 00:20:51.863
And I say,

00:20:53.150 --> 00:20:55.943
it's the only way to make
it work for you really well.

00:20:58.314 --> 00:21:03.314
I'm excited to share it
with all of you volunteers,

00:21:03.314 --> 00:21:06.806
because I think you're
the most serious people

00:21:06.806 --> 00:21:08.700
in the whole world.

00:21:08.700 --> 00:21:10.850
And I like serious people.

00:21:10.850 --> 00:21:12.000
There's a lot of people that

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:12.890
if I say

00:21:13.850 --> 00:21:16.010
let's fight our way through Nagarjuna's

00:21:16.010 --> 00:21:19.060
most difficult book about emptiness,

00:21:19.060 --> 00:21:21.110
because he understood tantra

00:21:21.110 --> 00:21:23.560
and he knew it was necessary
for Medicine Buddha.

00:21:25.280 --> 00:21:28.090
In fact, it's got 8,000 pages

00:21:28.090 --> 00:21:30.490
about his understanding of tantra

00:21:30.490 --> 00:21:32.163
in the database already.

00:21:33.210 --> 00:21:34.470
Let's think through it.

00:21:34.470 --> 00:21:35.720
So I trust you guys

00:21:38.560 --> 00:21:40.893
won't get confused or go crazy.

00:21:42.240 --> 00:21:43.610
We have to fight our way

00:21:43.610 --> 00:21:46.423
deep through emptiness. In the monastery,

00:21:47.630 --> 00:21:51.010
if the teacher can make you
confused about emptiness,

00:21:51.010 --> 00:21:52.977
they think it's progress.

00:21:53.870 --> 00:21:57.040
If you think you understand
emptiness after half an hour,

00:21:57.040 --> 00:21:57.873
you're wrong.

00:22:00.134 --> 00:22:02.710
It took me about 20 years or something.

00:22:02.710 --> 00:22:04.490
So here we go.

00:22:04.490 --> 00:22:07.923
We're going to go to
our actual text today.

00:22:09.960 --> 00:22:12.223
This is our deep dive class number seven.

00:22:13.140 --> 00:22:15.820
Here we go.

00:22:15.820 --> 00:22:17.030
All right, uncle Tim,

00:22:17.030 --> 00:22:18.477
are you ready with...

00:22:19.590 --> 00:22:21.630
This chapter,

00:22:21.630 --> 00:22:22.830
let's go to the chapter name.

00:22:24.850 --> 00:22:27.510
By the way we're well
into the text already.

00:22:28.690 --> 00:22:30.790
This is called Chapter 13,

00:22:30.790 --> 00:22:33.410
and it's "An investigation of Factors".

00:22:33.410 --> 00:22:37.210
Now, those sharp, sharp guys among you,

00:22:37.210 --> 00:22:40.260
you should tell grandpa,

00:22:40.260 --> 00:22:43.080
"Wait, we already did that in Chapter 1!".

00:22:43.080 --> 00:22:45.310
Well, what was the name of Chapter 1?

00:22:45.310 --> 00:22:47.220
An Investigation of

00:22:49.430 --> 00:22:50.273
Conditions.

00:22:51.341 --> 00:22:53.630
RKYEN BZHI, the four conditions.

00:22:53.630 --> 00:22:56.410
Now, 12 chapters later,

00:22:56.410 --> 00:22:59.360
he decides to cover factors?

00:22:59.360 --> 00:23:00.480
Well, what's the difference between

00:23:00.480 --> 00:23:02.420
a factor and a condition?

00:23:02.420 --> 00:23:03.253
Let's go back.

00:23:03.253 --> 00:23:04.340
Can you bring it up again?

00:23:06.480 --> 00:23:08.220
Yeah. 'DU BYED means

00:23:08.220 --> 00:23:10.410
things that make other things happen.

00:23:10.410 --> 00:23:14.190
Oftentimes 'DU BYED
means secondary causes,

00:23:14.190 --> 00:23:16.740
which is why I translated it as factors.

00:23:16.740 --> 00:23:18.940
For example, what's the
main cause of a tree?

00:23:19.980 --> 00:23:20.870
It's the seed.

00:23:20.870 --> 00:23:22.460
That's called NYER LEN GYI RGYU.

00:23:22.460 --> 00:23:25.020
That's called the immediate cause.

00:23:25.020 --> 00:23:27.140
And then you have 'DU BYED

00:23:27.140 --> 00:23:29.940
which means contributing factors

00:23:29.940 --> 00:23:33.480
like water, sunlight, fertilizer.

00:23:33.480 --> 00:23:34.990
What's BRTAG PA mean you guys?

00:23:34.990 --> 00:23:38.210
This is the chapter 'Investigation'.

00:23:38.210 --> 00:23:39.043
Oops.

00:23:39.043 --> 00:23:40.230
How do you stay in Sanskrit?

00:23:41.415 --> 00:23:42.698
- [Male student] Pariksha.

00:23:42.698 --> 00:23:43.833
- Pariksha.

00:23:43.833 --> 00:23:44.666
Pariksa,

00:23:44.666 --> 00:23:46.250
looking all around the question.

00:23:46.250 --> 00:23:48.440
'Pari', like periscope,

00:23:48.440 --> 00:23:50.610
'iksha', which came into German as

00:23:51.580 --> 00:23:53.320
'alga', which came into English as

00:23:53.320 --> 00:23:54.153
E-Y-E,

00:23:54.153 --> 00:23:56.610
that's why there's a
Y, in the English word

00:23:56.610 --> 00:23:57.513
for your eyeball.

00:23:58.510 --> 00:24:02.090
So each chapter of the 27 chapters

00:24:02.090 --> 00:24:03.850
in Nagarjuna's most difficult

00:24:03.850 --> 00:24:07.011
and most important work called...

00:24:07.011 --> 00:24:07.844
- [Male student] Pariksha.

00:24:07.844 --> 00:24:09.056
- No, his book.

00:24:09.056 --> 00:24:10.020
- [Male student] Prajna.

00:24:10.020 --> 00:24:11.000
- Just 'Wisdom'.

00:24:11.000 --> 00:24:13.350
And that's so Nagarjuna.

00:24:13.350 --> 00:24:18.350
He didn't say "A discussion
of the details of wisdom'.

00:24:18.680 --> 00:24:19.513
Somebody asked him,

00:24:19.513 --> 00:24:20.346
what's your book name?

00:24:20.346 --> 00:24:21.179
He said "Wisdom".

00:24:22.420 --> 00:24:23.253
- Yeah but what...

00:24:23.253 --> 00:24:24.120
- Wisdom.

00:24:24.120 --> 00:24:24.953
- But...

00:24:24.953 --> 00:24:26.430
- Wisdom.

00:24:26.430 --> 00:24:28.330
And that's so Nagarjuna.

00:24:29.810 --> 00:24:31.433
He's a man of few words.

00:24:32.630 --> 00:24:36.010
So we're going to investigate,

00:24:36.010 --> 00:24:38.010
how does one thing cause another thing.

00:24:38.010 --> 00:24:42.440
But this particular chapter

00:24:42.440 --> 00:24:43.670
is not named

00:24:44.790 --> 00:24:45.920
in an obvious way.

00:24:45.920 --> 00:24:49.403
In this case factors means illusion.

00:24:51.210 --> 00:24:53.690
So what's the connection

00:24:53.690 --> 00:24:56.450
between one thing causing another thing

00:24:56.450 --> 00:24:58.010
and the idea of an illusion,

00:24:58.010 --> 00:25:00.150
'maya', maya, an illusion.

00:25:00.150 --> 00:25:03.253
So really he should have
called this maya pariksha,

00:25:04.250 --> 00:25:07.610
It's not really discussing the
different kinds of factors.

00:25:07.610 --> 00:25:10.070
It did that already in the first chapter.

00:25:10.070 --> 00:25:12.170
By Chapter 13,

00:25:12.170 --> 00:25:16.360
he's talking about how
do causes and conditions,

00:25:16.360 --> 00:25:18.973
how are they involved with illusion?

00:25:19.950 --> 00:25:21.323
So here we go.

00:25:22.480 --> 00:25:23.533
Put on your seatbelt.

00:25:26.070 --> 00:25:28.020
And by the way,

00:25:28.020 --> 00:25:31.300
he's not satisfied with
covering illusion. At the end,

00:25:31.300 --> 00:25:35.427
he covers STONG NYID KYI STONG PA

00:25:35.427 --> 00:25:37.036
STONG PA NYID KYI STONG PA

00:25:37.036 --> 00:25:38.029
- [Female student] The
emptiness of living beings?

00:25:38.029 --> 00:25:39.610
- The emptiness of emptiness.

00:25:39.610 --> 00:25:42.260
So you guys this morning,

00:25:42.260 --> 00:25:43.140
you have bad luck.

00:25:43.140 --> 00:25:44.503
You got on a rocket ship.

00:25:46.716 --> 00:25:47.549
We're going to talk about

00:25:47.549 --> 00:25:50.423
the emptiness of emptiness
by the time we finish today.

00:25:52.030 --> 00:25:55.750
And I'll keep coming back to
the Medicine Buddha practice,

00:25:55.750 --> 00:25:56.980
and showing why,

00:25:56.980 --> 00:26:00.173
if you understand emptiness,

00:26:02.100 --> 00:26:03.700
your mantras will be more powerful

00:26:03.700 --> 00:26:05.036
and your practice will be more...

00:26:05.036 --> 00:26:07.190
and you'll just be super
Medicine Buddha guy.

00:26:07.190 --> 00:26:08.023
Okay?

00:26:08.023 --> 00:26:09.120
All right, here we go.

00:26:10.020 --> 00:26:14.060
First verse, Mr. Tim.

00:26:14.060 --> 00:26:16.093
,BCOM LDAN 'DAS KYIS CHOS GANG ZHIG

00:26:16.093 --> 00:26:18.059
,SLU BA DE NI BRDZUN ZHES GSUNGS,

00:26:18.059 --> 00:26:20.259
,'DU BYED THAMS CAD SLU BA'I CHOS,

00:26:20.259 --> 00:26:22.867
,DES NA DE DAG BRDZUN PA YIN,

00:26:22.867 --> 00:26:24.433
BCOM LDAN 'DAS KYIS CHOS GANG ZHIG

00:26:24.433 --> 00:26:25.540
The Buddha said,

00:26:25.540 --> 00:26:27.202
every single thing in the world

00:26:27.202 --> 00:26:29.990
SLU BA - cheats you.

00:26:29.990 --> 00:26:32.610
Everything in the world cheats you.

00:26:32.610 --> 00:26:35.600
The mantras of Medicine
Buddha also cheat you.

00:26:35.600 --> 00:26:36.453
What?

00:26:37.750 --> 00:26:39.700
Then I raise a 'why?'

00:26:39.700 --> 00:26:40.695
Why?

00:26:40.695 --> 00:26:42.178
Because BRDZUN PA

00:26:42.178 --> 00:26:43.800
They lie to you.

00:26:43.800 --> 00:26:45.217
They lie to you.

00:26:46.299 --> 00:26:48.194
Everything in the world is cheating you.

00:26:48.194 --> 00:26:49.027
Why?

00:26:49.027 --> 00:26:50.280
Because they lie to you.

00:26:50.280 --> 00:26:52.780
BRDZUN PA GSUNGS, said the Buddha.

00:26:52.780 --> 00:26:54.080
Now, there's a very...

00:26:54.080 --> 00:26:55.160
I'm just going to get you ready,

00:26:55.160 --> 00:26:57.400
if you ever get to the monastery

00:26:57.400 --> 00:27:00.560
and you're ever debating in a colloquial

00:27:00.560 --> 00:27:02.623
Tibetan at 2000 words a second,

00:27:03.840 --> 00:27:06.943
somebody might bring
up this favorite topic.

00:27:07.878 --> 00:27:11.164
SANGS RGYAS KYIS BRDZUN GSUNGS

00:27:11.164 --> 00:27:15.650
It says here BCOM LDAN
'DAS KYIS BRDZUN GSUNGS

00:27:17.240 --> 00:27:18.863
The Buddha spoke lie.

00:27:22.800 --> 00:27:25.203
The Buddha spoke "lies".

00:27:26.632 --> 00:27:29.840
Okay.

00:27:29.840 --> 00:27:31.923
- So the Buddha doesn't follow
the 10 good deeds, right?

00:27:31.923 --> 00:27:33.120
- What do you mean?

00:27:33.120 --> 00:27:34.300
- He broke number four.

00:27:34.300 --> 00:27:35.250
- What's number four?

00:27:36.310 --> 00:27:37.791
- He's lying.

00:27:37.791 --> 00:27:40.470
The Buddha spoke lies.

00:27:40.470 --> 00:27:42.350
And if you want to have a fun debate

00:27:42.350 --> 00:27:45.300
with one of the 12 year
olds at the monastery,

00:27:45.300 --> 00:27:48.708
this is good for like an
hour and a half or something.

00:27:48.708 --> 00:27:52.541
[mimicking small child voice]

00:27:54.220 --> 00:27:55.120
"Buddha spoke lies!"

00:27:57.950 --> 00:27:59.790
Here's where he spoke lies.

00:27:59.790 --> 00:28:01.470
In Nagarjuna, he spoke lies.

00:28:01.470 --> 00:28:03.430
But what does it really mean?

00:28:03.430 --> 00:28:08.430
He said all things which
have causes are lying to you.

00:28:08.530 --> 00:28:10.580
So he just mentioned the word lie,

00:28:10.580 --> 00:28:11.723
he didn't speak a lie.

00:28:12.600 --> 00:28:15.110
He spoke "lies",

00:28:15.110 --> 00:28:16.500
but he didn't say a lie.

00:28:16.500 --> 00:28:17.650
Got it?

00:28:17.650 --> 00:28:18.483
It's a joke.

00:28:19.380 --> 00:28:20.213
All right.

00:28:20.213 --> 00:28:22.446
If you're ever debating
with the 12 year olds,

00:28:22.446 --> 00:28:23.310
you can note it.

00:28:23.310 --> 00:28:25.050
'DU BYED THAMS CAD SLU BA'I CHOS.

00:28:25.050 --> 00:28:26.670
Everything that has a cause,

00:28:26.670 --> 00:28:28.210
or everything that is a cause,

00:28:28.210 --> 00:28:29.720
is lying to you.

00:28:29.720 --> 00:28:31.040
Therefore...

00:28:31.040 --> 00:28:32.120
Sorry.

00:28:32.120 --> 00:28:34.410
Everything that has a
cause is cheating you,

00:28:34.410 --> 00:28:37.350
therefore they are liars, BRDZUN PA

00:28:37.350 --> 00:28:38.728
They are liars.

00:28:41.388 --> 00:28:45.310
This is how Nagarjuna starts the chapter.

00:28:45.310 --> 00:28:48.920
And that's why we had Tim and Grandpa

00:28:48.920 --> 00:28:52.533
in the picture at the
beginning of the class.

00:28:56.660 --> 00:28:58.620
And the idea is that,

00:28:58.620 --> 00:28:59.610
I don't know,

00:28:59.610 --> 00:29:04.610
the employee is cheating
the employer, I guess.

00:29:06.080 --> 00:29:08.640
And he got caught.

00:29:08.640 --> 00:29:12.670
So the idea is

00:29:12.670 --> 00:29:16.160
the employee is cheating the employer,

00:29:16.160 --> 00:29:17.970
and therefore he will have to

00:29:19.170 --> 00:29:20.500
lie to the employer.

00:29:20.500 --> 00:29:23.400
So there's a connection
between cheating and lying.

00:29:23.400 --> 00:29:25.590
He stole the money, which is cheating.

00:29:25.590 --> 00:29:27.150
And now he's going to
have to lie about it,

00:29:27.150 --> 00:29:28.810
to keep the money.

00:29:28.810 --> 00:29:30.330
All right, so just get in that mood.

00:29:30.330 --> 00:29:31.890
We're talking about illusion.

00:29:31.890 --> 00:29:34.670
We're talking about somebody lying to you.

00:29:34.670 --> 00:29:36.770
All right, let's go to
the next verse, Tim.

00:29:42.259 --> 00:29:44.051
,GAL TE SLU CHOS GANG YIN PA,

00:29:44.051 --> 00:29:45.967
,DE BRDZUN DE LA CI ZHIG SLU,

00:29:45.967 --> 00:29:48.250
,BCOM LDAN 'DAS KYIS DE GSUNGS PA,

00:29:48.250 --> 00:29:50.940
,STONG NYID YONGS SU BSTAN PA YIN,

00:29:50.940 --> 00:29:53.040
Look, okay I agree.

00:29:53.040 --> 00:29:55.836
So suppose everything's cheating me.

00:29:55.836 --> 00:29:58.335
DE BRDZUN DE LA CI ZHIG SLU

00:29:58.335 --> 00:30:00.190
Then what's it lying about?

00:30:00.190 --> 00:30:04.760
How do things, including
Medicine Buddha practice

00:30:04.760 --> 00:30:07.000
and including Medicine Buddha mantra,

00:30:07.000 --> 00:30:09.250
how are they lying to me?

00:30:09.250 --> 00:30:10.841
How are they lying to me?

00:30:10.841 --> 00:30:12.870
BCOM LDAN 'DAS KYIS DE GSUNGS PA

00:30:12.870 --> 00:30:15.180
Look, he said they are lying to you.

00:30:15.180 --> 00:30:19.180
And that got him into the subject
of STONG NYID - emptiness.

00:30:20.980 --> 00:30:22.880
- Wow, what did he mean?

00:30:22.880 --> 00:30:27.880
- Well, the honesty of
that employee's transaction

00:30:30.750 --> 00:30:31.583
don't exist.

00:30:32.660 --> 00:30:34.350
He's cheating the company.

00:30:34.350 --> 00:30:37.210
How much honesty is in his transaction?

00:30:37.210 --> 00:30:38.710
How much honesty is going on

00:30:38.710 --> 00:30:40.840
at that desk at that moment?

00:30:40.840 --> 00:30:41.673
Zero.

00:30:41.673 --> 00:30:44.360
And that's called emptiness. Got it?

00:30:44.360 --> 00:30:46.520
When somebody lies to you,

00:30:46.520 --> 00:30:48.490
there's no reality there.

00:30:48.490 --> 00:30:51.960
Then the situation is empty of reality.

00:30:51.960 --> 00:30:55.050
When someone cheats you, they lie to you.

00:30:55.050 --> 00:30:56.420
When they lie to you,

00:30:56.420 --> 00:30:57.700
the truth is gone.

00:30:57.700 --> 00:31:01.030
And that's a kind of emptiness.

00:31:01.030 --> 00:31:04.000
If it's not real, it's empty.

00:31:04.000 --> 00:31:06.510
Buddha said things that cheat you,

00:31:06.510 --> 00:31:07.580
lie to you.

00:31:07.580 --> 00:31:09.880
Everything around you is cheating you.

00:31:09.880 --> 00:31:12.920
Everything around you, including
Medicine Buddha mantras,

00:31:12.920 --> 00:31:14.640
is lying to you.

00:31:14.640 --> 00:31:16.460
And therefore it's all empty.

00:31:16.460 --> 00:31:18.090
There's no truth there.

00:31:18.090 --> 00:31:19.740
Nothing's real.

00:31:19.740 --> 00:31:20.573
Got it?

00:31:21.590 --> 00:31:24.528
All right, then...

00:31:24.528 --> 00:31:26.020
I don't know...

00:31:26.020 --> 00:31:27.670
I was trying to find
a picture about lying,

00:31:27.670 --> 00:31:28.553
here it is.

00:31:29.980 --> 00:31:31.740
It's a Gucci bag

00:31:31.740 --> 00:31:35.820
that you buy in Thailand on the street

00:31:35.820 --> 00:31:37.040
for $2.

00:31:37.040 --> 00:31:38.100
There's a place in,

00:31:38.100 --> 00:31:39.404
oh no, it's in Bejing,

00:31:39.404 --> 00:31:40.654
there's a special market.

00:31:41.510 --> 00:31:42.750
My friend went crazy,

00:31:42.750 --> 00:31:45.860
my friend from Israel,
he went to this market.

00:31:45.860 --> 00:31:50.100
He bought like 30 Gucci
bags for all his relatives.

00:31:50.100 --> 00:31:51.910
And they're each like a dollar.

00:31:51.910 --> 00:31:55.190
You pick them up and the
handle falls off them,

00:31:55.190 --> 00:31:56.688
stuff like that.

00:31:56.688 --> 00:31:58.840
So it looks like a Gucci bag,

00:31:58.840 --> 00:32:00.660
but it's a fake Gucci bag.

00:32:00.660 --> 00:32:02.090
And the Buddha said

00:32:02.090 --> 00:32:03.840
everything around you is like that,

00:32:03.840 --> 00:32:05.327
everything's lying to you.

00:32:06.240 --> 00:32:09.210
Let's go to the next verse.

00:32:09.210 --> 00:32:10.043
Oh, sorry.

00:32:10.043 --> 00:32:14.282
I'm going to throw a quotation
and it's not in your...

00:32:17.060 --> 00:32:20.800
So when did the Buddha talk about lying?

00:32:20.800 --> 00:32:23.390
Supposedly the Buddha
has talked about lying.

00:32:23.390 --> 00:32:25.350
So can you show me the quotation?

00:32:25.350 --> 00:32:27.640
And Choney Lama takes the challenge

00:32:27.640 --> 00:32:28.780
and he says, "I'll show you the quote.

00:32:28.780 --> 00:32:31.150
I got a quotation where
Buddha talked about it"

00:32:31.150 --> 00:32:35.400
And it's called MA DROS PAS ZHUS PA LAS

00:32:35.400 --> 00:32:40.060
MA DROS PA means a special
lake that will never dry out.

00:32:40.060 --> 00:32:41.230
DROS PA means dry out.

00:32:41.230 --> 00:32:43.888
MA DROS PA means can never dry out.

00:32:43.888 --> 00:32:46.230
Anavatapta

00:32:46.230 --> 00:32:48.630
in Sanskrit, Anavatapta,

00:32:48.630 --> 00:32:52.240
which means, sometimes
it's called not warm,

00:32:52.240 --> 00:32:54.490
but there's a naga living in the lake.

00:32:54.490 --> 00:32:58.250
His name is MA DROS PA - Anavatapta.

00:32:58.250 --> 00:33:02.083
Sometimes they call it not warm or warm.

00:33:02.990 --> 00:33:07.340
And he's having a conversation
with Lord Buddha in this sutra.

00:33:07.340 --> 00:33:10.350
It's the sutra of the naga in the lake.

00:33:10.350 --> 00:33:12.550
And he says, Buddha says,

00:33:12.550 --> 00:33:14.391
,GANG ZHIG RKYEN LAS SKYES PA DE MA SKYES,

00:33:14.391 --> 00:33:17.073
,DE LA SKYE BA'I RANG BZHIN YOD MA YIN,

00:33:17.073 --> 00:33:21.220
Anything that comes from conditions...

00:33:21.220 --> 00:33:22.700
There's our conditions.

00:33:22.700 --> 00:33:24.680
Anything that comes from
causes and conditions

00:33:24.680 --> 00:33:27.810
like seeds or water or fertilizer,

00:33:27.810 --> 00:33:32.460
anything that's born from water and seeds,

00:33:32.460 --> 00:33:33.653
is never born.

00:33:34.860 --> 00:33:39.630
Anything that is born from
water and seeds is not born.

00:33:39.630 --> 00:33:42.010
Buddha said, "It's all fake.

00:33:42.010 --> 00:33:43.949
It's all a lie."

00:33:43.949 --> 00:33:45.870
DE LA SKYE BA'I RANG BZHIN YOD MA YIN

00:33:45.870 --> 00:33:48.897
There's no nature of being born there.

00:33:48.897 --> 00:33:50.113
Nothing's being born. There's no

00:33:50.113 --> 00:33:52.920
the slightest bit of being born there.

00:33:52.920 --> 00:33:55.430
RKYEN LA RAG LAS GANG DE STONG BAR BSHAD

00:33:55.430 --> 00:34:00.430
I tell you, anything that's
mixed up with causes is empty.

00:34:01.170 --> 00:34:02.860
It's a lie.

00:34:02.860 --> 00:34:04.640
The truth is gone.

00:34:04.640 --> 00:34:07.380
GANG ZHIG STONG NYID SHES DE BAG YOD YIN

00:34:07.380 --> 00:34:10.940
Anybody who really understands that

00:34:10.940 --> 00:34:13.025
can do stuff well,

00:34:13.025 --> 00:34:15.579
like Medicine Buddha
practice, BAG YOD YIN.

00:34:15.579 --> 00:34:19.200
You know, BAG YOD means like a new born...

00:34:19.200 --> 00:34:20.960
like a new wed woman,

00:34:20.960 --> 00:34:21.890
something like that.

00:34:21.890 --> 00:34:24.720
It means they are skillful.

00:34:24.720 --> 00:34:28.250
They are living in the right way.

00:34:28.250 --> 00:34:30.270
Anyone who understands emptiness

00:34:31.310 --> 00:34:34.550
is doing a good Medicine Buddha practice.

00:34:34.550 --> 00:34:35.383
Who said that?

00:34:35.383 --> 00:34:36.370
The Buddha said that.

00:34:36.370 --> 00:34:37.203
Why?

00:34:37.203 --> 00:34:39.710
Because they understand
the illusion there.

00:34:39.710 --> 00:34:41.750
They understand that
there's emptiness there.

00:34:41.750 --> 00:34:44.473
And that's where the
Buddha described lies.

00:34:45.820 --> 00:34:48.140
Anything that has a cause is lying to you.

00:34:48.140 --> 00:34:49.920
If you get it,

00:34:49.920 --> 00:34:51.740
then you can live a good life.

00:34:51.740 --> 00:34:53.070
You can have a good practice.

00:34:53.070 --> 00:34:54.420
Got it?

00:34:54.420 --> 00:34:56.110
All right, I went and found it for you.

00:34:56.110 --> 00:34:58.960
I'll put it in the
translation when I finish it.

00:34:58.960 --> 00:35:01.350
By the way, translation
is already 400 pages,

00:35:01.350 --> 00:35:02.660
and it's tough.

00:35:02.660 --> 00:35:04.430
It's really tough.

00:35:04.430 --> 00:35:07.920
We're going through it at
about 110 miles an hour.

00:35:09.830 --> 00:35:12.061
It should take 20 years or something.

00:35:12.061 --> 00:35:12.894
All right, here we go.

00:35:12.894 --> 00:35:13.727
Next verse.

00:35:14.590 --> 00:35:16.140
It's really a verse and a half by the way.

00:35:18.610 --> 00:35:22.340
What did I say is tricky
about reading Nagarjuna?

00:35:22.340 --> 00:35:23.660
What did I say

00:35:23.660 --> 00:35:25.392
could trip you up?

00:35:25.392 --> 00:35:28.580
- [Male student] (indiscernible)

00:35:28.580 --> 00:35:29.413
- Yeah.

00:35:29.413 --> 00:35:31.700
Sometimes it sprinkles in
the other guy's comments,

00:35:31.700 --> 00:35:33.350
and he doesn't warn you.

00:35:33.350 --> 00:35:35.350
There's no warning.

00:35:35.350 --> 00:35:37.580
And you need Choney Lama to tell you,

00:35:37.580 --> 00:35:39.460
"No, no, this is not Nagarjuna.

00:35:39.460 --> 00:35:41.182
This is the other guy."

00:35:41.182 --> 00:35:42.033
So here's the other guy;

00:35:42.033 --> 00:35:43.974
,DNGOS RNAMS NGO BO NYID MED DE,

00:35:43.974 --> 00:35:45.949
,GZHAN DU 'GYUR BA SNANG PHYIR RO,

00:35:45.949 --> 00:35:48.182
,DNGOS PO NGO BO NYID MED MED,

00:35:48.182 --> 00:35:49.966
,GANG PHYIR DNGOS RNAMS STONG PA NYID,

00:35:49.966 --> 00:35:51.423
,GAL TE NGO BO NYID MED NA,

00:35:51.423 --> 00:35:53.660
,GZHAN DU 'GYUR BA GANG GI YIN,

00:35:53.660 --> 00:35:55.943
Here's the other guy.

00:35:55.943 --> 00:35:58.060
DNGOS RNAMS NGO BO NYID MED DE

00:35:58.060 --> 00:36:01.840
If stuff doesn't have a
true nature of its own,

00:36:01.840 --> 00:36:05.310
if things don't have a
true nature of their own,

00:36:05.310 --> 00:36:07.640
Nagarjuna says they don't, by the way,

00:36:07.640 --> 00:36:08.650
He says,

00:36:08.650 --> 00:36:11.706
if things don't have a
true nature of their own,

00:36:11.706 --> 00:36:13.110
GZHAN DU 'GYUR BA SNANG PHYIR RO

00:36:13.110 --> 00:36:14.653
then why do they change?

00:36:18.710 --> 00:36:19.543
And by the way,

00:36:19.543 --> 00:36:22.320
the example is going
to be when you use milk

00:36:22.320 --> 00:36:23.300
to make yogurt.

00:36:23.300 --> 00:36:25.550
In India,

00:36:25.550 --> 00:36:27.830
the way you make yogurt in the market is

00:36:28.850 --> 00:36:32.300
you get a bowl of hot milk,

00:36:32.300 --> 00:36:36.000
you put in the yeast from the last yogurt,

00:36:36.000 --> 00:36:37.800
and then you're hang it up in your shop.

00:36:37.800 --> 00:36:40.930
And the flies cover it for the whole day.

00:36:40.930 --> 00:36:42.210
You can't even see the white color.

00:36:42.210 --> 00:36:43.530
It's all black.

00:36:43.530 --> 00:36:45.353
And then they serve it the next day.

00:36:46.850 --> 00:36:49.880
When I got back from India,

00:36:49.880 --> 00:36:52.263
the doctor told me I had
17 kinds of parasites.

00:36:54.190 --> 00:36:55.900
So anyway,

00:36:55.900 --> 00:36:59.340
the milk transforms into yogurt.

00:36:59.340 --> 00:37:02.660
Can you tell the difference
between the yogurt and the milk?

00:37:02.660 --> 00:37:03.493
Yeah, it's different.

00:37:03.493 --> 00:37:04.465
It tastes different.

00:37:04.465 --> 00:37:07.650
It's sticky, right?

00:37:07.650 --> 00:37:10.110
Then the other guy says
an interesting thing.

00:37:10.110 --> 00:37:13.300
He says, look, if things that have causes

00:37:13.300 --> 00:37:14.980
have no nature of their own,

00:37:14.980 --> 00:37:16.473
then how can they change?

00:37:19.760 --> 00:37:22.530
If the milk didn't have an identity,

00:37:22.530 --> 00:37:25.180
then how did it drop that
identity and become a yogurt?

00:37:26.179 --> 00:37:27.850
Got it?

00:37:27.850 --> 00:37:30.630
So according to you, Nagarjuna,

00:37:30.630 --> 00:37:32.260
if everything's empty,

00:37:32.260 --> 00:37:34.400
and it has no nature of its own,

00:37:34.400 --> 00:37:36.700
then milk can never change.

00:37:36.700 --> 00:37:39.200
Because it has to have a nature to change.

00:37:39.200 --> 00:37:40.540
It has to be something

00:37:40.540 --> 00:37:42.320
before it can change into something else.

00:37:42.320 --> 00:37:43.790
If it's not something in the first place,

00:37:43.790 --> 00:37:45.040
how can it become yogurt?

00:37:46.647 --> 00:37:47.760
GZHAN DU 'GYUR BA SNANG PHYIR RO

00:37:47.760 --> 00:37:49.373
We can see things change.

00:37:50.389 --> 00:37:52.920
DNGOS PO NGO BO NYID MED MED

00:37:52.920 --> 00:37:54.920
Therefore, it's not true

00:37:54.920 --> 00:37:56.857
that nothing has any nature of it's own.

00:37:56.857 --> 00:37:58.110
MED MED

00:37:58.110 --> 00:38:00.703
It's not true that things have no nature.

00:38:01.755 --> 00:38:05.390
GANG PHYIR DNGOS RNAMS STONG PA NYID

00:38:05.390 --> 00:38:06.892
Okay, say things are empty.

00:38:06.892 --> 00:38:08.242
GAL TE NGO BO NYID MED NA

00:38:08.242 --> 00:38:11.246
If the milk doesn't have
a nature of being milk,

00:38:11.246 --> 00:38:12.660
GZHAN DU 'GYUR BA GANG GI YIN

00:38:12.660 --> 00:38:14.410
well, how can it become yogurt?

00:38:14.410 --> 00:38:16.690
How can it drop its former identity

00:38:16.690 --> 00:38:18.260
and take on a new identity

00:38:18.260 --> 00:38:20.410
if it never had an identity?

00:38:20.410 --> 00:38:21.800
This is the other guy

00:38:21.800 --> 00:38:22.900
talking to Nagarjuna.

00:38:24.710 --> 00:38:27.460
And if you don't know it's the
other guy, you're in trouble.

00:38:31.090 --> 00:38:33.550
And I found a picture that I like:

00:38:35.080 --> 00:38:38.150
it's leaves, green and
different colored leaves.

00:38:38.150 --> 00:38:38.983
It's...

00:38:38.983 --> 00:38:39.816
I don't know.

00:38:39.816 --> 00:38:40.740
It's springtime here.

00:38:40.740 --> 00:38:43.410
We're thinking about leaves and...

00:38:43.410 --> 00:38:45.430
If the leaf wasn't green,

00:38:45.430 --> 00:38:46.803
how could it turn yellow?

00:38:48.760 --> 00:38:49.840
Got it?

00:38:49.840 --> 00:38:52.410
If the leaf wasn't green,

00:38:52.410 --> 00:38:54.103
how could it turn yellow?

00:38:54.103 --> 00:38:55.320
- Nagarjuna,

00:38:55.320 --> 00:38:58.500
you said nothing has
any nature of its own.

00:38:58.500 --> 00:39:00.150
- Okay, I did.

00:39:00.150 --> 00:39:01.503
- So leaves aren't green?

00:39:04.750 --> 00:39:06.280
- What's that got to do with anything?

00:39:06.280 --> 00:39:07.740
- Well, if they're not green,

00:39:07.740 --> 00:39:08.903
how can they turn yellow?

00:39:08.903 --> 00:39:10.643
Then how can you say 'turn'?

00:39:11.820 --> 00:39:13.630
They must be green.

00:39:13.630 --> 00:39:15.403
Those green leaves are green.

00:39:16.660 --> 00:39:17.650
They have a nature.

00:39:17.650 --> 00:39:18.800
They're green.

00:39:18.800 --> 00:39:20.140
If they didn't have a nature,

00:39:20.140 --> 00:39:21.540
they couldn't become yellow.

00:39:22.690 --> 00:39:24.750
It makes sense right?

00:39:24.750 --> 00:39:25.690
Got it?

00:39:25.690 --> 00:39:27.343
Yes, you're correct.

00:39:29.930 --> 00:39:31.503
All right, here we go.

00:39:32.400 --> 00:39:33.253
Next verse,

00:39:34.841 --> 00:39:35.674
,GAL TE NGO BO NYID YOD NA,

00:39:35.674 --> 00:39:40.674
,CI LTA BUR NA GZHAN DU 'GYUR,

00:39:43.627 --> 00:39:46.610
And Nagarjuna's answer is, "No.

00:39:46.610 --> 00:39:49.590
If things did have a nature,
how could they change?"

00:39:53.080 --> 00:39:54.310
The other guy said,

00:39:54.310 --> 00:39:56.470
if green leaves aren't green,

00:39:56.470 --> 00:39:58.350
how can they turn to yellow?

00:39:58.350 --> 00:39:59.930
And then Nagarjuna says,

00:39:59.930 --> 00:40:01.900
if green leaves were green,

00:40:01.900 --> 00:40:03.750
they couldn't turn to yellow.

00:40:03.750 --> 00:40:05.993
Your argument defeats yourself.

00:40:07.030 --> 00:40:08.840
If green leaves are green,

00:40:08.840 --> 00:40:09.803
they can't become yellow leaves.

00:40:09.803 --> 00:40:11.023
They're green.

00:40:11.890 --> 00:40:14.350
You can't call it yellow
a green leaf. Come on.

00:40:14.350 --> 00:40:16.003
If a green leaf was really green,

00:40:16.880 --> 00:40:18.550
it couldn't become yellow.

00:40:18.550 --> 00:40:20.750
So don't give me this stupid example that,

00:40:20.750 --> 00:40:22.350
because things change,

00:40:22.350 --> 00:40:24.590
they must have had some nature

00:40:24.590 --> 00:40:26.230
because you couldn't say they changed

00:40:26.230 --> 00:40:28.400
if they didn't have a
nature in the first place

00:40:28.400 --> 00:40:30.320
to change from.

00:40:30.320 --> 00:40:31.153
Got it?

00:40:31.153 --> 00:40:31.986
You okay?

00:40:31.986 --> 00:40:33.280
Just keep nodding.

00:40:33.280 --> 00:40:35.460
You guys at home just keep nodding.

00:40:36.615 --> 00:40:37.860
CI LTA BUR NA GZHAN DU 'GYUR

00:40:37.860 --> 00:40:41.027
So he uses the argument
back to the other guy.

00:40:41.027 --> 00:40:44.330
If green leaves are green,

00:40:44.330 --> 00:40:45.760
then they can't become yellow leaves,

00:40:45.760 --> 00:40:47.862
because they're green leaves.

00:40:47.862 --> 00:40:48.950
Got it?

00:40:48.950 --> 00:40:50.810
He uses the same argument back to the guy.

00:40:50.810 --> 00:40:52.303
Here's the picture.

00:40:56.000 --> 00:40:57.390
This picture was easy to find.

00:40:57.390 --> 00:40:59.650
Okay, if green leaves are green,

00:40:59.650 --> 00:41:01.220
they can never be yellow.

00:41:01.220 --> 00:41:02.830
Duh.

00:41:02.830 --> 00:41:05.000
If green leaves had a nature

00:41:05.000 --> 00:41:06.460
of being green,

00:41:06.460 --> 00:41:08.010
they could never become yellow leaves.

00:41:09.350 --> 00:41:10.470
The other guy said,

00:41:10.470 --> 00:41:13.090
if they don't have a
nature of being green,

00:41:13.090 --> 00:41:15.870
how can you observe a change in them

00:41:15.870 --> 00:41:18.043
if they drop that nature
and become yellow?

00:41:19.120 --> 00:41:19.953
Got it?

00:41:19.953 --> 00:41:21.000
So they must have had a nature.

00:41:22.650 --> 00:41:23.673
All right, now,

00:41:24.580 --> 00:41:27.740
Choney Lama uses a very
beautiful word here

00:41:27.740 --> 00:41:30.750
and I want to use it
for our Sanskrit lesson.

00:41:30.750 --> 00:41:33.750
So every Nagarjuna class we have,

00:41:33.750 --> 00:41:37.950
we're going to do a mini Sanskrit lesson.

00:41:37.950 --> 00:41:40.150
So you've got to learn a
little bit of Sanskrit.

00:41:40.150 --> 00:41:42.840
Don't worry, it won't hurt you.

00:41:42.840 --> 00:41:45.480
It's like 15 words for the whole course.

00:41:45.480 --> 00:41:48.770
But since you have to
speak in Sanskrit later,

00:41:48.770 --> 00:41:50.690
after the Medicine Buddha practice,

00:41:50.690 --> 00:41:51.920
which has no nature,

00:41:51.920 --> 00:41:54.150
makes you a Medicine Buddha,

00:41:54.150 --> 00:41:56.570
you're going to have to speak Sanskrit.

00:41:56.570 --> 00:41:59.070
So you might as well
go get used to it now.

00:41:59.070 --> 00:41:59.903
It's like you're going to Guadalajara,

00:41:59.903 --> 00:42:02.330
you might as well learn about five words.

00:42:02.330 --> 00:42:04.080
It makes the taxi drivers so happy.

00:42:05.960 --> 00:42:07.100
All right.

00:42:07.100 --> 00:42:08.870
So here we go.

00:42:08.870 --> 00:42:10.633
You got that one from me, you guys?

00:42:11.510 --> 00:42:13.890
This is our little Sanskrit lesson.

00:42:13.890 --> 00:42:15.410
This is a word called...

00:42:15.410 --> 00:42:17.380
By the way I misspelled it there, Tim,

00:42:17.380 --> 00:42:18.700
is it too late to fix it?

00:42:18.700 --> 00:42:21.660
Prakirti, it should be K-I-R.

00:42:21.660 --> 00:42:24.863
This is an old mistake
that everyone else makes.

00:42:26.232 --> 00:42:27.770
Prakirti.

00:42:27.770 --> 00:42:30.050
And those of you may have heard it.

00:42:30.050 --> 00:42:31.950
You've probably heard this 'prakirti',

00:42:31.950 --> 00:42:36.380
it's a very famous word
in Hindu yoga schools.

00:42:36.380 --> 00:42:37.850
It's a very famous idea.

00:42:39.660 --> 00:42:42.340
In Tibetan it's called GSHIS LUGS

00:42:42.340 --> 00:42:43.936
GSHIS LUGS

00:42:43.936 --> 00:42:44.769
Say GSHIS LUGS

00:42:44.769 --> 00:42:45.602
- [Class in unison] GSHIS LUGS

00:42:45.602 --> 00:42:46.435
- [GMR] GSHIS LUGS

00:42:46.435 --> 00:42:47.268
- [Class in unison] GSHIS LUGS

00:42:47.268 --> 00:42:49.850
And that GSHIS is a very unusual word

00:42:49.850 --> 00:42:53.367
that means 'the primordial
nature' or something.

00:42:53.367 --> 00:42:54.200
GSHIS

00:42:54.200 --> 00:42:57.193
And it happens to be used
in a famous expression

00:42:58.484 --> 00:43:01.210
BKRA SHIS BDE LEGS

00:43:01.210 --> 00:43:05.107
which means are you having
a good primordial nature?

00:43:05.107 --> 00:43:07.630
[GMR laughs]

00:43:07.630 --> 00:43:10.540
And that's how you say "hi" in Tibetan.

00:43:10.540 --> 00:43:11.520
You say BKRA SHIS BDE LEGS

00:43:11.520 --> 00:43:15.113
which means wonderful
primordial shining nature.

00:43:16.731 --> 00:43:17.797
BKRA SHIS BDE LEGS

00:43:17.797 --> 00:43:19.280
When you say "thank you" in Tibetan,

00:43:19.280 --> 00:43:20.113
what's it mean?

00:43:20.113 --> 00:43:21.363
THUGS RJE CHE

00:43:21.363 --> 00:43:22.810
- [Female student] (indiscernible)

00:43:22.810 --> 00:43:24.278
- You're great heart.

00:43:24.278 --> 00:43:26.570
You're great holy heart.

00:43:26.570 --> 00:43:27.937
It's how you say "thank you".

00:43:28.840 --> 00:43:32.140
And how you say "good morning"

00:43:32.140 --> 00:43:34.500
is "shining primordial nature

00:43:34.500 --> 00:43:36.043
of happiness and goodness".

00:43:37.450 --> 00:43:41.080
Which used to be the expression for

00:43:41.080 --> 00:43:42.700
Happy New Year.

00:43:42.700 --> 00:43:44.360
And then it became so common

00:43:44.360 --> 00:43:46.950
that people started using
it for good morning.

00:43:46.950 --> 00:43:47.783
Alright.

00:43:49.140 --> 00:43:51.959
Prakirti comes from pra-,

00:43:51.959 --> 00:43:53.860
the prefix letter pra-,

00:43:53.860 --> 00:43:55.670
and then kirti.

00:43:55.670 --> 00:43:58.720
And by the way people say
"prakriti" and it's wrong.

00:43:58.720 --> 00:44:00.313
The pronunciation is wrong.

00:44:01.610 --> 00:44:03.640
Prakrit, people say prakrit,

00:44:03.640 --> 00:44:05.390
and that's like saying,

00:44:06.230 --> 00:44:07.920
it's like your German friends who say

00:44:07.920 --> 00:44:09.820
"I went and bought cheap (Jeep)

00:44:09.820 --> 00:44:10.883
and drove it home."

00:44:13.160 --> 00:44:15.303
It's just a mistake of pronunciation.

00:44:16.405 --> 00:44:19.265
All right, so pra- means forward,

00:44:19.265 --> 00:44:20.800
or very much.

00:44:20.800 --> 00:44:23.020
√kṛ is the verbal root that means

00:44:23.020 --> 00:44:24.373
to make or to do.

00:44:26.140 --> 00:44:28.270
We spoke about pra- many times.

00:44:28.270 --> 00:44:29.500
√kṛ we spoke about,

00:44:29.500 --> 00:44:31.390
it's found in 'cereal',

00:44:31.390 --> 00:44:33.520
'create' and 'karma'.

00:44:33.520 --> 00:44:36.420
And the C in cereal used to be K.

00:44:36.420 --> 00:44:38.570
It changed around the time of Shakespeare.

00:44:40.950 --> 00:44:45.573
And then -ta makes it a past tense.

00:44:46.512 --> 00:44:48.000
And I think it came into English

00:44:48.000 --> 00:44:49.030
with E-D:

00:44:49.030 --> 00:44:49.983
made it,

00:44:52.955 --> 00:44:54.153
or I created - '-ed', '-ted'.

00:44:55.600 --> 00:45:00.600
So prakirti means that which
was made from the beginning.

00:45:01.200 --> 00:45:05.000
And it means the original
nature of an object.

00:45:05.000 --> 00:45:06.540
In Sankhya philosophy,

00:45:06.540 --> 00:45:10.110
in ancient Hindu yoga philosophy,

00:45:10.110 --> 00:45:14.883
they will juxtapose two things.

00:45:16.900 --> 00:45:18.436
Ms. Kasica:

00:45:18.436 --> 00:45:19.646
prakirti and...

00:45:19.646 --> 00:45:21.567
- [Ms. Kasica] Parusha

00:45:21.567 --> 00:45:22.400
- Parusha

00:45:22.400 --> 00:45:24.140
Prakirti and parusha

00:45:24.140 --> 00:45:28.660
So 'parusha' means the Person.

00:45:28.660 --> 00:45:30.900
And it means God,

00:45:30.900 --> 00:45:32.410
the Person, capital P,

00:45:32.410 --> 00:45:33.400
who made everything.

00:45:33.400 --> 00:45:36.760
And then prakirti is the nature
which was made by the God.

00:45:36.760 --> 00:45:41.760
So in Hinduism, especially in
the ancient yoga philosophy

00:45:41.870 --> 00:45:44.140
prakirti is nature

00:45:44.140 --> 00:45:46.730
and parusha is the creator.

00:45:46.730 --> 00:45:48.070
But in Buddhism,

00:45:48.070 --> 00:45:50.030
prakirti means the nature,

00:45:50.030 --> 00:45:52.030
which things can not have.

00:45:52.030 --> 00:45:53.610
The original nature,

00:45:53.610 --> 00:45:55.300
green leaf.

00:45:55.300 --> 00:45:58.150
Green is in the leaf, like that.

00:45:58.150 --> 00:45:59.960
So try to remember that.

00:45:59.960 --> 00:46:01.820
That's called GSHIS LUGS.

00:46:01.820 --> 00:46:04.610
And Choney Lama is very
skillful to use the word.

00:46:04.610 --> 00:46:07.403
So now, today you learned a new word:

00:46:09.031 --> 00:46:11.891
prakirti, that which was
made in the beginning.

00:46:11.891 --> 00:46:14.863
Pra- kirti and the nature of things.

00:46:17.210 --> 00:46:21.330
When Michael was made by his parents,

00:46:21.330 --> 00:46:24.753
was he made with a nature
built in from the factory?

00:46:25.800 --> 00:46:28.540
Did he have a nature prakirti in him

00:46:28.540 --> 00:46:30.600
from the factory?

00:46:30.600 --> 00:46:32.033
From my mom factory.

00:46:33.340 --> 00:46:34.173
Alright, here we go.

00:46:34.173 --> 00:46:35.033
Next subject.

00:46:38.683 --> 00:46:40.091
,DE NYID LA NI GZHAN 'GYUR MED,

00:46:40.091 --> 00:46:41.682
,GZHAN NYID LA YANG YOD MA YIN,

00:46:41.682 --> 00:46:43.499
,GANG PHYIR GZHON NU MI RGA STE,

00:46:43.499 --> 00:46:46.397
,GANG PHYIR RGAS PA'ANG MI RGA'O,

00:46:46.397 --> 00:46:49.405
Now Nagarjuna, he's got...

00:46:49.405 --> 00:46:51.280
He just jumps on you.

00:46:51.280 --> 00:46:53.650
- Hey, you guys're talking
about change, right?

00:46:53.650 --> 00:46:55.060
Green leaf changes yellow, right?

00:46:55.060 --> 00:46:56.140
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:46:56.140 --> 00:46:57.423
- Does that have a nature?

00:46:58.420 --> 00:47:00.470
Does the changing have a nature?

00:47:00.470 --> 00:47:01.303
Got it?

00:47:01.303 --> 00:47:03.410
Folks forget the leaf now.

00:47:03.410 --> 00:47:05.340
Did the green leaf have a nature?

00:47:05.340 --> 00:47:06.703
We say no. They say yes.

00:47:07.730 --> 00:47:12.140
They say it had to have a
nature because it changed.

00:47:12.140 --> 00:47:13.890
If it didn't have an identity,

00:47:13.890 --> 00:47:16.480
how could it take on a new
identity of being yellow?

00:47:16.480 --> 00:47:18.040
How could milk change,

00:47:18.040 --> 00:47:21.210
drop its old identity and become yogurt

00:47:21.210 --> 00:47:23.650
if it didn't have an
identity in the first place.

00:47:23.650 --> 00:47:25.960
Now we say, "By the way,

00:47:25.960 --> 00:47:28.560
you guys want to talk about
the emptiness of change?"

00:47:29.440 --> 00:47:31.500
When the milk becomes yogurt,

00:47:31.500 --> 00:47:33.653
when the leaf turns to yellow,

00:47:33.653 --> 00:47:35.103
what's the emptiness of that?

00:47:35.981 --> 00:47:38.100
DE NYID LA NI GZHAN 'GYUR MED

00:47:38.100 --> 00:47:43.100
If things have a primordial
nature, prakirti,

00:47:43.157 --> 00:47:43.990
GZHAN 'GYUR MED

00:47:43.990 --> 00:47:45.652
they cannot change to something else.

00:47:45.652 --> 00:47:48.380
GZHAN NYID LA YANG YOD MA YIN

00:47:48.380 --> 00:47:51.253
If things are self-existently separate,

00:47:52.610 --> 00:47:53.860
they can't have a nature

00:47:54.840 --> 00:47:58.410
if things are self-existently
separate or other.

00:47:58.410 --> 00:48:01.103
Is the yellow leaf different
from the green leaf?

00:48:04.310 --> 00:48:05.263
Yeah, it's yellow.

00:48:06.320 --> 00:48:08.680
Is the yogurt different from the milk?

00:48:08.680 --> 00:48:09.513
Yeah.

00:48:09.513 --> 00:48:11.153
Is that difference self-existent?

00:48:13.556 --> 00:48:14.870
GANG PHYIR GZHON NU MI RGA STE

00:48:14.870 --> 00:48:16.770
Young people don't get old,

00:48:16.770 --> 00:48:18.763
and old people don't get old either.

00:48:20.160 --> 00:48:21.820
That's Nagarjuna.

00:48:21.820 --> 00:48:23.670
Young people don't get old,

00:48:23.670 --> 00:48:25.930
and old people don't get old either.

00:48:25.930 --> 00:48:28.560
Now let's do the second
one because it's easier.

00:48:28.560 --> 00:48:30.020
- Do old people get old?

00:48:30.020 --> 00:48:31.220
- No, they're already old.

00:48:33.340 --> 00:48:35.200
- Okay, we got that one finished.

00:48:35.200 --> 00:48:36.500
Now the big question is,

00:48:36.500 --> 00:48:38.700
do young people get old?

00:48:38.700 --> 00:48:40.300
- No, because they're young people.

00:48:45.390 --> 00:48:46.930
- Okay, listen.

00:48:46.930 --> 00:48:48.360
Do young people get old?

00:48:48.360 --> 00:48:49.500
- No.

00:48:49.500 --> 00:48:50.333
- Why?

00:48:50.333 --> 00:48:51.166
- They're young.

00:48:55.080 --> 00:48:56.020
Yeah, it's separate.

00:48:56.020 --> 00:48:57.120
It's totally separate.

00:48:58.190 --> 00:49:00.130
- Do old people get old?

00:49:00.130 --> 00:49:01.747
- No, they are already old.

00:49:01.747 --> 00:49:03.040
- Do young people get old?

00:49:03.040 --> 00:49:04.073
- No, they're young.

00:49:05.090 --> 00:49:06.430
- Got it?

00:49:06.430 --> 00:49:08.110
- Quit fooling around with the words!

00:49:08.110 --> 00:49:10.080
- I'm not fooling around with words.

00:49:10.080 --> 00:49:11.970
I'm trying to demonstrate to you

00:49:11.970 --> 00:49:13.620
that words are messed up already

00:49:13.620 --> 00:49:15.445
and you don't notice it.

00:49:16.343 --> 00:49:17.240
- Young got old.

00:49:17.240 --> 00:49:18.732
- What are you talking about?

00:49:18.732 --> 00:49:20.943
Young old, an old young person?

00:49:21.906 --> 00:49:23.380
What do you mean?

00:49:23.380 --> 00:49:24.640
- Something's wrong.

00:49:24.640 --> 00:49:26.850
The mantra cured the cancer.

00:49:26.850 --> 00:49:30.400
Yhe Medicine Buddha
mantra cured the cancer.

00:49:30.400 --> 00:49:32.250
- What's the connection?

00:49:32.250 --> 00:49:34.050
- The mantra never touched the cancer.

00:49:36.900 --> 00:49:38.380
How can it cure the cancer?

00:49:38.380 --> 00:49:39.823
Are they separate or not?

00:49:40.923 --> 00:49:42.739
,GAL TE DE NYID GZHAN 'GYUR NA,

00:49:42.739 --> 00:49:44.700
,'O MA NYID NI ZHOR 'GYUR RO,

00:49:44.700 --> 00:49:46.968
How does milk become ZHO?

00:49:46.968 --> 00:49:49.233
ZHO means yogurt.

00:49:51.765 --> 00:49:54.310
If you ever get hungry ask for some ZHO

00:49:54.310 --> 00:49:57.040
but say low tone ZHO.

00:49:57.040 --> 00:49:58.461
Don't say SHO

00:49:58.461 --> 00:49:59.340
SHO means dice

00:49:59.340 --> 00:50:02.373
and it means you want to lose some money.

00:50:03.350 --> 00:50:04.220
Don't say, I'm hungry,

00:50:04.220 --> 00:50:08.145
I need some SHO - ZHO -  ZHO.

00:50:08.145 --> 00:50:09.985
,O MA NYID NI ZHOR 'GYUR RO,

00:50:09.985 --> 00:50:11.768
,'O MA LAS GZHAN GANG ZHIG NI,

00:50:11.768 --> 00:50:13.684
,ZHO YI DNGOS PO YIN PAR 'GYUR,

00:50:13.684 --> 00:50:18.680
Is the milk separate
from the yogurt or not?

00:50:19.530 --> 00:50:20.780
Are they separate things?

00:50:22.670 --> 00:50:24.090
Yes or no?

00:50:24.090 --> 00:50:25.140
I'm not tricking you.

00:50:26.000 --> 00:50:26.833
Here's Nagarjuna,

00:50:26.833 --> 00:50:27.666
typical Nagarjuna,

00:50:27.666 --> 00:50:29.010
"Hey I'm not tricking you.

00:50:29.010 --> 00:50:30.860
Just answer the question."

00:50:30.860 --> 00:50:32.173
Is the milk the yogurt?

00:50:33.349 --> 00:50:34.182
- [Female student] No.

00:50:34.182 --> 00:50:35.015
- Are they separate?

00:50:35.015 --> 00:50:35.990
- [Female students] Yes.

00:50:35.990 --> 00:50:37.103
- Do they ever touch?

00:50:39.580 --> 00:50:40.760
Cannot.

00:50:40.760 --> 00:50:42.380
Why?

00:50:42.380 --> 00:50:44.340
The milk was yesterday.

00:50:44.340 --> 00:50:45.683
The yogurt is today.

00:50:46.960 --> 00:50:48.293
They can't overlap.

00:50:49.760 --> 00:50:53.660
If they touch at any point,

00:50:53.660 --> 00:50:55.263
then yesterday is today.

00:50:57.060 --> 00:50:58.750
It's not possible.

00:50:58.750 --> 00:51:01.450
Milk cannot turn into yogurt.

00:51:01.450 --> 00:51:02.283
It's not possible.

00:51:02.283 --> 00:51:03.663
Something weird is going on.

00:51:04.510 --> 00:51:07.270
Medicine Buddha mantra cannot cure cancer,

00:51:07.270 --> 00:51:08.253
but it does.

00:51:10.061 --> 00:51:12.653
And that's how we get yogurt, right?

00:51:12.653 --> 00:51:14.370
How many times you ate yogurt?

00:51:14.370 --> 00:51:17.853
There must be something
there. All right, next.

00:51:18.700 --> 00:51:22.350
I have a picture of a
grandma and granddaughter.

00:51:23.824 --> 00:51:27.698
The granddaughter is not old,

00:51:27.698 --> 00:51:30.218
getting old.

00:51:30.218 --> 00:51:31.313
And the grandma's not getting old,

00:51:31.313 --> 00:51:33.700
because the grandma already got old.

00:51:33.700 --> 00:51:35.580
And the daughter's young.

00:51:35.580 --> 00:51:36.973
All right, go figure it out.

00:51:38.270 --> 00:51:39.570
Next one.

00:51:39.570 --> 00:51:41.428
Huh, this class is going to...

00:51:41.428 --> 00:51:42.270
Let's see.

00:51:42.270 --> 00:51:45.100
Now, according to Choney Lama,

00:51:45.100 --> 00:51:46.220
who's guiding us,

00:51:46.220 --> 00:51:47.570
and by the way

00:51:47.570 --> 00:51:49.640
we haven't gone through the commentary.

00:51:49.640 --> 00:51:52.460
Commentary would take about
20 years to teach, really.

00:51:52.460 --> 00:51:53.980
And it's beautiful.

00:51:53.980 --> 00:51:56.820
But he warns us.

00:51:56.820 --> 00:51:58.347
Choney Lama says,

00:51:58.347 --> 00:52:01.000
STONG NYID RANG BZHIN GYIS
YOD PA'I SGRUB BYED DGAG PA'O

00:52:01.000 --> 00:52:03.790
I'm going to prove to you that emptiness

00:52:03.790 --> 00:52:06.480
doesn't have a nature of it's own.

00:52:06.480 --> 00:52:07.380
I'm going to prove to you

00:52:07.380 --> 00:52:09.310
the emptiness is empty.

00:52:09.310 --> 00:52:11.223
And that's his big thing.

00:52:12.920 --> 00:52:16.730
The next verse is one of
the most famous verses

00:52:16.730 --> 00:52:18.150
of this whole book.

00:52:18.150 --> 00:52:20.330
And it's kind of an honor

00:52:20.330 --> 00:52:22.760
that we have all our Medicine Buddha

00:52:22.760 --> 00:52:25.630
and ACI volunteers here today

00:52:25.630 --> 00:52:29.050
because we hit maybe the most,

00:52:29.050 --> 00:52:32.110
well, second most famous
verse from this whole book.

00:52:32.110 --> 00:52:34.900
And it's just cool that you're here,

00:52:34.900 --> 00:52:36.760
because in five years,

00:52:36.760 --> 00:52:38.290
it's only going to happen once.

00:52:38.290 --> 00:52:39.123
So here we go.

00:52:40.182 --> 00:52:42.065
,GAL TE STONG MIN CUNG ZAD YOD,

00:52:42.065 --> 00:52:43.556
,STONG PA CUNG ZAD YOD PAR 'GYUR,

00:52:43.556 --> 00:52:46.656
,MI STONG CUNG ZAD YOD MIN NA,

00:52:46.656 --> 00:52:48.597
,STONG PA YOD PAR GA LA 'GYUR,

00:52:48.597 --> 00:52:51.120
GAL TE STONG MIN CUNG ZAD YOD

00:52:51.120 --> 00:52:53.760
If there's anything that's not empty,

00:52:53.760 --> 00:52:56.999
if there's the slightest
thing which is not empty,

00:52:56.999 --> 00:52:58.610
STONG PA CUNG ZAD YOD PAR 'GYUR

00:52:58.610 --> 00:53:00.960
you could have the
slightest thing which isn't.

00:53:03.900 --> 00:53:06.873
If there's the slightest
thing which isn't empty,

00:53:07.780 --> 00:53:10.373
then you can have the
slightest bit of emptiness.

00:53:12.353 --> 00:53:14.430
MI STONG CUNG ZAD YOD MIN NA

00:53:14.430 --> 00:53:17.801
If there isn't the slightest
thing which is not empty,

00:53:17.801 --> 00:53:19.330
STONG PA YOD PAR GA LA 'GYUR

00:53:19.330 --> 00:53:23.010
how could you have emptiness?

00:53:23.010 --> 00:53:26.240
You need the opposite to define a thing.

00:53:26.240 --> 00:53:29.260
If there's no such thing
as not being empty,

00:53:29.260 --> 00:53:31.473
how are you going to recognize emptiness?

00:53:32.570 --> 00:53:36.100
You recognize things by
comparison to other things.

00:53:36.100 --> 00:53:37.420
How do you know something's blue

00:53:37.420 --> 00:53:38.420
if it's not yellow?

00:53:41.697 --> 00:53:43.280
If blue was around you all the time,

00:53:43.280 --> 00:53:44.770
if everything in your room was blue

00:53:44.770 --> 00:53:46.070
you wouldn't see the blue.

00:53:47.610 --> 00:53:48.770
I mean, you'd be looking at it,

00:53:48.770 --> 00:53:49.970
but you wouldn't see it.

00:53:51.700 --> 00:53:56.670
So this is a very famous proof

00:53:56.670 --> 00:53:58.533
that emptiness has its own emptiness.

00:54:00.925 --> 00:54:01.758
Now, how is that?

00:54:03.430 --> 00:54:04.780
Let's look at this picture.

00:54:11.120 --> 00:54:12.810
This is a glass of water,

00:54:12.810 --> 00:54:14.680
which is completely full.

00:54:14.680 --> 00:54:16.663
It's definitely not empty,

00:54:17.800 --> 00:54:21.340
but there would have to
be some part of non-empty,

00:54:21.340 --> 00:54:23.433
if the emptiness came from its own side.

00:54:24.701 --> 00:54:28.230
If emptiness came from its own side,

00:54:28.230 --> 00:54:29.350
there would have to be part

00:54:29.350 --> 00:54:30.490
which is not empty.

00:54:30.490 --> 00:54:33.320
Therefore, that last statement was...

00:54:33.320 --> 00:54:34.653
Who was talking?

00:54:36.610 --> 00:54:38.870
Sounds like the other guy.

00:54:38.870 --> 00:54:40.170
Sounds like the other guy.

00:54:41.500 --> 00:54:42.730
Okay, Nagarjuna,

00:54:42.730 --> 00:54:45.030
So must be some stuff...

00:54:45.030 --> 00:54:48.270
If things don't have an
identity of their own,

00:54:48.270 --> 00:54:49.990
then the only way you're
going to recognize it

00:54:49.990 --> 00:54:51.250
is by looking at the opposite.

00:54:51.250 --> 00:54:54.330
Therefore, there must be
some things in the universe

00:54:54.330 --> 00:54:55.650
that aren't empty,

00:54:55.650 --> 00:54:57.537
and you can compare them to
the things that are empty,

00:54:57.537 --> 00:54:59.590
and you can tell they're empty.

00:54:59.590 --> 00:55:01.090
Otherwise, how could you ever see -

00:55:01.090 --> 00:55:03.213
if emptiness didn't have its own nature?

00:55:04.510 --> 00:55:06.523
If it were only empty by comparison.

00:55:08.520 --> 00:55:09.960
Okay, here we go.

00:55:09.960 --> 00:55:11.420
If you're not confused yet,

00:55:11.420 --> 00:55:12.270
we'll work on it.

00:55:15.800 --> 00:55:17.150
Let's go to the next verse.

00:55:18.643 --> 00:55:20.567
,RGYAL BA RNAMS KYIS STONG PA NYID,

00:55:20.567 --> 00:55:23.451
,LTA KUN NGES PAR 'BYUNG BAR GSUNGS,

00:55:23.451 --> 00:55:25.817
,GANG DAG STONG PA NYID LTA BA,

00:55:25.817 --> 00:55:28.317
,DE DAG BSGRUB TU MED PAR GSUNGS,

00:55:28.317 --> 00:55:30.970
This is a very subtle verse,

00:55:30.970 --> 00:55:32.603
it takes a lot of work.

00:55:34.970 --> 00:55:36.540
I'll introduce it to you.

00:55:36.540 --> 00:55:38.290
And what my teacher said was

00:55:38.290 --> 00:55:39.970
you have to cook it.

00:55:39.970 --> 00:55:42.213
Rebecca used to sit with my teacher.

00:55:43.320 --> 00:55:44.740
"You cook it."

00:55:44.740 --> 00:55:46.050
We said, "No, no, we don't
understand anything."

00:55:46.050 --> 00:55:47.543
"Cook it, God damn, cook it.

00:55:48.860 --> 00:55:49.693
I'm going home."

00:55:50.600 --> 00:55:52.000
I should try that.

00:55:52.000 --> 00:55:54.152
RGYAL BA RNAMS KYIS STONG PA NYID

00:55:54.152 --> 00:55:58.151
The victors stated about emptiness,

00:55:58.151 --> 00:55:59.480
LTA KUN NGES PAR 'BYUNG

00:55:59.480 --> 00:56:00.980
This NGES 'BYUNG

00:56:00.980 --> 00:56:01.980
- first principle path -

00:56:03.700 --> 00:56:05.000
is renunciation.

00:56:05.000 --> 00:56:08.783
But it also means to rip something out,

00:56:10.160 --> 00:56:11.231
to rip something,

00:56:11.231 --> 00:56:12.064
NGES PAR 'BYUNG

00:56:12.064 --> 00:56:12.940
pull it out.

00:56:12.940 --> 00:56:15.226
Pull yourself out of the home life

00:56:15.226 --> 00:56:16.340
is called renunciation.

00:56:16.340 --> 00:56:17.373
But here,

00:56:21.023 --> 00:56:23.717
the Buddha said that emptiness rips out

00:56:23.717 --> 00:56:27.860
LTA KUN, LOG LTA - wrong views.

00:56:27.860 --> 00:56:29.790
They said if you get emptiness,

00:56:29.790 --> 00:56:32.750
it will renunciate your wrong views.

00:56:32.750 --> 00:56:33.740
Pull them out of the house,

00:56:33.740 --> 00:56:36.083
get out. This house [points to his head].

00:56:40.742 --> 00:56:43.550
GANG DAG STONG PA NYID LTA BA

00:56:43.550 --> 00:56:45.013
This is very subtle.

00:56:46.280 --> 00:56:48.253
Whosoever sees emptiness.

00:56:49.790 --> 00:56:52.150
Whosoever thinks they see emptiness

00:56:54.210 --> 00:56:55.870
being from its own side.

00:56:55.870 --> 00:56:57.280
That's the trick.

00:56:57.280 --> 00:57:00.040
Whosoever sees emptiness,

00:57:00.040 --> 00:57:01.270
DE DAG BSGRUB TU MED PAR GSUNGS

00:57:01.270 --> 00:57:04.020
This BSGRUB means fixable,

00:57:04.020 --> 00:57:06.165
repairable. MED

00:57:08.880 --> 00:57:11.600
What's the biggest mistake
you can make in life?

00:57:11.600 --> 00:57:14.423
If you think that emptiness
has its own nature.

00:57:16.050 --> 00:57:17.710
Then you are hopeless.

00:57:17.710 --> 00:57:19.070
Truly hopeless.

00:57:19.070 --> 00:57:21.317
Who said that? GSUNGS - the Buddha.

00:57:22.890 --> 00:57:25.380
If you think the mantra is going to work

00:57:25.380 --> 00:57:26.940
from it's own side,

00:57:26.940 --> 00:57:28.100
you are hopeless.

00:57:28.100 --> 00:57:29.143
Totally hopeless.

00:57:30.120 --> 00:57:32.313
It's better you didn't hear the mantra.

00:57:33.500 --> 00:57:35.430
If you're going to grab onto the mantra

00:57:35.430 --> 00:57:36.880
as working from its own side,

00:57:36.880 --> 00:57:39.163
and you don't need to save life

00:57:40.130 --> 00:57:42.050
for the mantra to work...

00:57:42.050 --> 00:57:42.883
Okay?

00:57:42.883 --> 00:57:43.740
If you think the mantra is going to work

00:57:43.740 --> 00:57:47.215
from its own side
without saving life, then

00:57:47.215 --> 00:57:51.740
you're going around saying
mantras without saving life -

00:57:51.740 --> 00:57:52.653
good luck.

00:57:53.720 --> 00:57:55.070
You're hopeless.

00:57:55.070 --> 00:57:55.903
Who said that?

00:57:56.800 --> 00:57:57.646
Buddha.

00:57:57.646 --> 00:57:59.670
BSGRUB TU MED PAR here means,

00:57:59.670 --> 00:58:03.130
you are broken and no one can fix you.

00:58:03.130 --> 00:58:03.963
Why?

00:58:03.963 --> 00:58:06.070
Because you're using the dharma already,

00:58:06.070 --> 00:58:07.423
but you're using it wrong.

00:58:08.660 --> 00:58:11.023
So you're the worst kind of broken.

00:58:12.070 --> 00:58:13.860
And I can't do anything for you.

00:58:13.860 --> 00:58:14.970
I can't fix you.

00:58:14.970 --> 00:58:16.300
Who said that?

00:58:16.300 --> 00:58:17.647
Buddha said that.

00:58:18.880 --> 00:58:19.713
Pretty heavy.

00:58:20.650 --> 00:58:23.000
So that finishes our class today.

00:58:23.000 --> 00:58:27.110
Again, it's a special
treat class suffering for

00:58:28.440 --> 00:58:30.680
those of you who have
been helping so much.

00:58:30.680 --> 00:58:35.680
And I know I helped my Lama for 30 years.

00:58:36.090 --> 00:58:38.450
I washed dishes for 30 years.

00:58:38.450 --> 00:58:41.740
Me and Elly found a picture of us

00:58:41.740 --> 00:58:43.920
shoveling snow outside,

00:58:43.920 --> 00:58:47.203
when it used to snow
before the global warming.

00:58:50.230 --> 00:58:52.040
That was the whole day. It was like that.

00:58:52.040 --> 00:58:55.520
So I got to tell you

00:58:55.520 --> 00:58:59.680
that being a volunteer is the coolest,

00:58:59.680 --> 00:59:01.500
smartest thing you can do.

00:59:01.500 --> 00:59:04.403
Really, honestly, I'm not just selfish.

00:59:05.627 --> 00:59:07.247
And I did it for 30 years.

00:59:07.247 --> 00:59:09.680
And I look back at those times,

00:59:09.680 --> 00:59:11.340
some of my friends from Princeton,

00:59:11.340 --> 00:59:12.173
they used to say,

00:59:12.173 --> 00:59:14.272
"That guy is taking advantage of you,

00:59:14.272 --> 00:59:16.530
"you're working all day for free.

00:59:16.530 --> 00:59:18.450
"You could be a big lawyer

00:59:18.450 --> 00:59:20.280
"or you could be a big
government official."

00:59:20.280 --> 00:59:21.980
They're all dead now.

00:59:21.980 --> 00:59:22.960
Or they got cancer

00:59:22.960 --> 00:59:26.040
and they write me letters
every day, all day.

00:59:26.040 --> 00:59:27.290
"Help me, help me,

00:59:27.290 --> 00:59:28.700
"I don't know what to do,

00:59:28.700 --> 00:59:30.530
teach me something."

00:59:30.530 --> 00:59:33.650
These guys told me, when
I went to my teacher,

00:59:33.650 --> 00:59:36.620
you're a fool to spend all day

00:59:36.620 --> 00:59:38.260
volunteering for your teacher.

00:59:38.260 --> 00:59:40.570
But I look back at those days...

00:59:40.570 --> 00:59:42.630
I look back at those days

00:59:42.630 --> 00:59:45.430
and I was really, really happy.

00:59:45.430 --> 00:59:47.189
Those were the happiest days of my life.

00:59:47.189 --> 00:59:51.456
So you are very smart to be a volunteer.

00:59:51.456 --> 00:59:52.773
And keep going.

00:59:53.620 --> 00:59:55.100
And you'll look back at these days

00:59:55.100 --> 00:59:55.940
and you'll say,

00:59:55.940 --> 00:59:57.939
oh, that was the best time of my life.

00:59:57.939 --> 00:59:59.627
All right. See you later.

